cropping/scaling and distinguishing template-owned colors from source-filled holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:18:#     - recolor 规则固定为“变成分隔条颜色”，线索完全来自可见结构，不依赖颜色 id、排序或隐藏状态。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:27:#       坐标来自输入而非输出，否则 recolor 后 bar 会彼此融合、无法再反推。实现中先从输入收集 bar，再统一回写。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:28:#     - ext-side 打点必须先于 recolor 执行；若先 recolor，输出虽然同样可写出，但逻辑上会把“源颜色”概念弄混。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:37:#     - recolor 目标不是任意映射，而是结构上唯一显眼的分隔条颜色；2-3 组样例即可支持人类归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:113:    # all bar coordinates must be collected from the input before recoloring, because the recolor step\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:129:    # D5 recolor: once the extension is complete, every source bar becomes the separator color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:280:        recolored = [(length, sep_color) for length, _color in bars]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:281:        _place_bars(expected, row, sep_col, bars_on_left, recolored, sep_gap)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D5/1/code.py:287:    # Variant guard: at least one bar pixel must recolor to the separator color in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D12/1/code.py:32:#   detection, 5-step travel, hit recolor, and collision painting remain unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D12/1/code.py:50:# - `hit_components` assumes landing on any occupied cell of a component recolors that whole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D12/1/code.py:246:    - Landing on a sprite recolors the whole hit sprite to maroon (9). Landing on empty background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/D1/4/code.py:7:# - Variant detail: 凹槽面积各不相同，工具按总面积排序，第k大的工具匹配第k大凹槽面积的框架。解题者需对两组对象分别排序后建立序数映射。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:3:# Name: 显式分割线 + 连接器匹配 + 箭头标记反射\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:28:#   3. Reflection is read from arrow glyphs inside the matched target quadrant:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:29:#      right-arrow => LR flip, down-arrow => UD flip. Quadrant position no longer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:35:#     * connector + only down-arrow -> copy there, but apply UD instead of LR;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:36:#     * connector + both arrows -> copy there with both flips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:59:#   arrows are instruction artifacts. They are stripped before motifs are stamped.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:66:#   regions are large enough for anchors, arrow glyphs, and at least one-cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:70:# - Active target anchors reserve a top band for arrows and at least one extra row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:77:#   3. read the arrows in those same quadrants to decide the reflection bits.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:83:# - Colors are function-separated: divider=1, anchors=2, arrows=3, bg=4,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:97:#   quadrants with both a connector color repeated in TL and at least one arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:330:    Copy the TL motif into connector-matched regions, scaling by anchor size and mirroring by arrow markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:335:    - Each active target shares a repeated connector color with a TL-side connector stub, and that same target region also contains one or two green arrow glyphs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:339:    - Extract the TL motif while ignoring connector colors, then for each active target read its arrows: right-arrow means LR reflection, down-arrow means UD reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:342:    Key insight: The divider only tells you where the four regions are; connector colors decide which anchors participate at all, and arrow glyphs independently decide how each matched copy is reflected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:561:def _paint_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, top: int, left: int, shape: frozenset[tuple[int, int]]) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:569:        _paint_arrow(grid, q_r0 + 1, q_c0 + 1, RIGHT_ARROW)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:571:        _paint_arrow(grid, q_r0 + 1, q_c0 + 5, DOWN_ARROW)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:23:      - 原题的对象类型不变：L 形箭头、单像素/3像素直线墙、对角线射线、遇墙反射。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:27:      - 每个箭头自带一个局部 3 色循环提示条；第 1/2/3/... 次反射后分别采用提示条第 1/2/3/... 个颜色，超出后循环。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:32:      - 箭头仍是单色 3 像素 L 形，2x2 bbox 缺一角。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:33:      - 每个箭头背后紧贴放一条 1x3 的多色提示条，顺序按 left->right 读取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:36:      - 若箭头沿 dr=1 发射，则提示条放在箭头 bbox 上方一行；dr=-1 时放在下方一行。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:37:      - 若箭头沿 dc=1 发射，则提示条比 bbox 向左多伸 1 格；dc=-1 时向右多伸 1 格。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:38:      - 这样提示条总在箭头“后侧”，且固定为水平 3 格，视觉上是局部图例而不是墙。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:40:      - 原题：箭头色 2 发射，碰到颜色 5 的墙后，反射点改成 5，后续段也用 5；再碰到颜色 7 的墙后改成 7。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:41:      - 变体：同样输入若箭头背后提示条是 [4,8,3]，则第一次反射后反射点改成 4、后续段也用 4；第二次反射改成 8；第三次反射改成 3；墙色只影响几何，不影响着色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/2/code.py:42:      - 差异落点：原 solver 在每个 bounce 分支里读取 wcol 并赋给 cur_col；变体要把这里改成读取箭头提示循环。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142c