/code.py:45:#     multiple trigger holes with the same row. The new solver records per-row beam lengths and asserts only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:56:# - The change is visible immediately: inputs contain multiple 5x5 solids instead\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D4/2/code.py:11:#   location, recolored with the shooter's own color, and translated by 1 cell in the shooter's firing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D4/2/code.py:15:#   This changes both color and coordinates, so the solver must infer a translation, not just a recolor mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D4/2/code.py:22:#   1. Old code could mark a hit by recoloring in place; new code cannot, so hit targets must be cleared first and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D4/2/code.py:37:#   repeat across the grid, so the recolor rule is inferable from 2-4 examples rather than looking arbitrary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D4/2/code.py:141:    - If the landing cell belongs to another sprite, recolor the whole struck sprite with the shooter's color and translate that entire 3-cell sprite by 1 cell in the same firing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/12/code.py:67:#      survive as a fixed color while other LR cells are recolored from LL.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/D3/0/code.py:7:# - Variant detail: 工具包含3种颜色：plug色、handle色和中间'铰链'色（1-2像素连接plug与handle）。铰链色在对接后变为背景色消失，仅plug和handle保留。解题者需识别三色结构并推断铰链的消失规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D2/3/code.py:29:#      placement detail only; the tiled copy still starts immediately across the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/3/code.py:25:#    - Input objects stay the same: 3-pixel L arrows plus colored wall pixels/segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D8/3/code.py:26:#    - Stage 1 still uses the original per-ray physics: each arrow traces diagonally,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi