e in the variant and must be replaced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:51:      - the reflection loop assumes the start cell is part of the arrow and that the ray begins from that cell; keeping the right-angle start avoids unrelated downstream changes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:52:      - arrow detection is still per-color connected-component based; to keep that safe, the generator forbids walls from using arrow colors, so no same-color wall can merge into an arrow component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:53:      - the new solver assumes a valid arrow bbox touches exactly one edge; the generator avoids corners so this assumption is always satisfied.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:55:    - left/right-edge arrows use row anchors in [1, H-3]; top/bottom-edge arrows use col anchors in [1, W-3], so no arrow touches two edges at once\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:56:    - occupied tracks arrows, planned rays, and walls, preventing overlap between objects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:60:    - because every arrow lives on the border, the \"source of direction\" is visible at a glance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:61:    - two arrows with identical missing-corner patterns but on different edges behave differently, making the D18 change observable rather than cosmetic\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:63:    - arrows are kept off corners and rays must contain at least 3 painted cells, so the border markers remain readable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:66:    - colors keep their original meaning: arrow color = initial ray color, wall color = inherited bounce color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D18/2/code.py:73:    Trace diagonal rays from border-anchored L-arrows, reflecting off colored walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new