:    Connect the plug sprite onto the base sprite, recolor the connectors to body color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D6/1/code.py:27:#     - remove the left strip and divider entirely by cropping, not by recoloring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D6/1/code.py:68:#     narrower and contain only the framed region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/14/code.py:28:#   Solver flow becomes: parse all Ts -> recolor every region exactly once -> count Ts -> rotate\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/14/code.py:31:#   population that already drives recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/14/code.py:39:#   Original `main()` assumed rotation could be decided after recoloring by reading an optional\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/14/code.py:55:#   recolored board is rotationally invariant, so the count cue actually changes the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/14/code.py:317:    - After all recoloring is resolved simultaneously, rotate the whole board by the total T count: 4 -> no rotation, 5 -> clockwise 90, 6 -> 180, 7 -> counterclockwise 90.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/D11/1/code.py:7:# - Variant detail: 第一个工具对接到框架后，其handle部分形成新的凹槽供第二个工具对接，形成嵌套结构。类似16b78196中的链式放置。解题者需识别迭代对接的终止条件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/2/code.py:109:    - Rectangle size still narrows the search, but repeated slot sizes are disambiguated by the guide pixels already shown inside each hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D9/2/code.py:32:  inner colors. It also places extra non-path frames so a requested target color can appear in multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D9/2/code.py:56:  the same next color exists in multiple directions, and only the direction token explains the chosen bridge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/0/code.py:58:     after ctrl recoloring, so the merged result remains legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/2/code.py:23:#     output: still recolor all ctrl pixels to obj after docking, but the output grid size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/2/code.py:68:#       no new color mapping burden beyond the original connector recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/2/code.py:155:    - Stamp the plug onto the base; recolor connectors from `ctrl` to `obj`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a25697e4/D11/2/code.py:7:# - Variant detail: 所有工具先对接到各自框架，然后整体执行第二步操作（如所有对接后的框架整体向某方向平移或居中）。两步操作解题者需串联理解。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/12/code.py:13:#   - the task runs in two recolor stages.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/12/code.py:25:#     recolors both together;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/12/code.py:26:#   - a flat one-stage \"legend directly sets each destination\" baseline would recolor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/12/code.py:65:# - The legend is reusable across multiple T markers, giving repeated evidence for the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/12/code.py:501:    - The legend strip, any small embedded scraps, and the optional L marker are erased into their touching owner region after the recoloring is complete. L orientation remains ┐ → CCW 90° and ┌ → CW 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D5/0/code.py:10:#     The output still places one template copy per lattice point and recolors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D5/0/code.py:52:#     on multiplicity, not order. That no longer holds; sequential painting is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D5/0/code.py:103:    - All remaining singletons share color O, the recolor used for the origin copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D6/0/code.py:26:#    the base connector, then recolor all ctrl to obj and tight-crop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/1/code.py:28:#        plug ctrl row  -> overlaps base obj, then later