/4/code.py:782:        witness_kind = \"tail\" if (n >= 5 and rng.random() < 0.65) else \"blocked\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:783:        if witness_kind == \"tail\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:784:            witness = _tail_witness_candidates(n, occupied, var_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/18/code.py:21:#     motif that splits into multiple 4-connected pieces because some links are only diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/18/code.py:78:      visible sprite can contribute multiple tally dots if its pixels are joined only diagonally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:17:#    - The input still has separator-defined sections and the output is still a recolored cropped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:23:#      original: [template | stencil | solid fg=8 | solid bg=3] -> crop template -> recolor with 8/3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:24:#      variant : [template | stencil | code [[8,3],[3,8]]]      -> decode diagonal rule -> recolor with 8/3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:35:#    - The recoloring/tile-repeat code still assumes a single cropped template mask and a background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:99:    - Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it using the decoded 2x2 symbol.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:101:    - Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D9/0/code.py:170:    - Stamp the template at every derived offset; the origin's own copy is recolored to O, and any multi-covered stamp pixels are also recolored to O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:18:#      output recolors ctrl -> obj and tight-crops the merged result.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/