instead of T, and repaint any pixel covered by multiple copies in O as well.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D4/0/code.py:275:    narrow = fa if int(fa[\"inner_size\"]) <= int(fb[\"inner_size\"]) else fb\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D4/0/code.py:276:    ia = narrow[\"inner_bbox\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:49:#     - Pixel-wise, the input shows only a narrow band cut from the motif, embedded inside a uniform padding color on a 20x20 canvas: for example a 4x18 row strip or an 18x4 column strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:67:#     - Humans can see the D2 change immediately because the input is no longer a block-like patch; it is a long narrow slice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:176:    - The non-padding strip is extremely elongated: a narrow horizontal band or a narrow vertical band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:185:    - The visible evidence is only a narrow band, so the meaningful support is the extracted strip rather than the whole padded canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D12/1/code.py:95:    - Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2, then repeat the recolored crop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D12/1/code.py:268:def _recolor_template(shape: np.ndarray, fg_color: int, accent_color: int, bg_color: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D12/1/code.py:286:    tile = _recolor_template(shape, fg_color, accent_color, bg_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D4/4/code.py:3:# Change: recolor + pattern_stamping — 原点stamp着O色，其余stamp着T色；重叠区域(total>=2)着O色 → stamp擦除模式\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D4/4/code.py:25:#       - the origin copy was recolored from T to O\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D4/4/code.py:26:#       - overlap regions were also recolored to O\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D4/4/code.py:37:#       - the center copy at delta (0,0) becomes O, so output contains a visibly recolored center sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D4/4/code.py:53:#     - old solver line \"paint everything T, then recolor origin/overlap to O\" is no longer valid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D4/4/code.py:62:#     - the output now uses only bg and T, so the D4 change is visible as topology rather than recolor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D4/4/code.py:86:    Key insight: The unique T singleton no longer says \"recolor this copy\" — it identifies which translated template instance should be missing entirely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D11/1/code.py:20:#      the center of a direct template stamp. There is no multiplication by template\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D11/1/code.py:44:#      few origin-only pixels, so both recoloring rules are visible from examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D11/1/code.py:109:    - Recolor the origin-centered copy to O, and recolor any multiply covered output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D14/1/code.py:21:#   (dr * h, dc * w), recolors the origin copy to O, and recolors overlaps to O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D14/1/code.py:47:# - Overlap recoloring cannot be done by directly painting per-copy colors, because a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D14/1/code.py:53:#   (multiples of h and w) still guarantees non-overlapping bboxes when stamps fit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D14/1/code.py:70:#   recolor/overlap color, and bg is the background. The variant changes geometry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D14/1/code.py:103:    - Paint the origin copy in O instead of T, and recolor any overlap area to O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D5/1/code.py:28:#         majority pattern, then recolor the minority-mask pixels to a third color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D3/2/code.py:109:    - In this variant, each non-blank source interior is itself made of multiple disconnected foreground components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D13/0/code.py:22:#   recolored to O, and overlaps also become O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D13/0/code.py:30:#   origin; the repeated singleton color is O, therefore it is also the recolor used\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D13/0/code.py:48:#   always O, and exactly one interior singleton is M. Because output recolors the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D13/0/code.py:53:#   (O), and the repeated color is the origin-stamp recolor. Generator constructs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D13/0/code.py:71:    - Paint covered cells as `T` by default, but recolor the origin copy and all multi-covered cells to `O`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/0/code.py:101:    - Crop the template to the bounding box of its non-black cells and recolor that crop with the two swatch colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/0/code.py:103:    - Repeat the recolored crop that many times with a one-cell background separator, but tile along the same direction as the blue separator lines themselves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/16/code.py:34:#    - Each sample uses 2-4 distinct templates, and every chosen template appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/16/code.py:64:#    - Multiple shape classes may share the same outside colors, which gives positive evidence that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/16/code.py:66:#    - Ranking depends only on the visible multiplicity of matching shapes. Ties are broken by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D4/3/code.py:62:#    - If multiple same-color targets are bridgeable, larger overlap and shorter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D10/0/code.py:146:    - The `T` singleton is the lattice origin and also identifies which stamped copy should be recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D10/0/code.py:151:    - Recolor the origin copy to `O`, and recolor any multiply covered cells to `O` as well.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D7/2/code.py:29:#      three bridge segments (four visited squares). Multiple crops and divider columns make the D7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D7/1/code.py:218:    - Paint all translated copies with T, then recolor the origin copy to O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D7/1/code.py:219:    - Any cell covered by multiple copies is also recolored to O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D5/3/code.py:47:#    swap rule visible across multiple locations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D5/3/code.py:54:#    a local 2-color inversion rather than a global recoloring table.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/3/code.py:183:    - Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black cells and recolor that crop with the two swatches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D10/1/code.py:40:#       from multiple structures.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D6/0/code.py:20:#     - output still stamps translated copies of the template on a coarse lattice, and recolors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D6/0/code.py:46:#       therefore singleton offsets must be exact multiples of the chosen gunit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D6/0/code.py:48:#     - overlap recoloring logic is unchanged, so coverage counting remains valid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D6/0/code.py:111:    - Recolor the origin's stamped copy to O, and recolor any overlap region to O as well.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/23/code.py:27:#   2. keep only non-red pixels whose row and col offsets from the anchor are multiples of 2,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D6/2/code.py:108:    - Stamp template copies at those normalized offsets scaled by the template bbox size; the origin copy and any overlap are recolored O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/2/code.py:90:#   - Foreground/background recoloring is still read directly from the swatches; colors do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/2/code.py:107:    - Crop block 1 to the bounding box of its non-black cells and recolor that crop with the two swatch colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/2/code.py:109:    - Tile the recolored crop with one background-colored spacer between copies; use a horizontal row of copies when the cropped template is wider than tall, a vertical stack when it is taller than wide, and horizontal for square crops.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D8/0/code.py:45:#    of multiple annotations on the same cells, so the grid stays clean.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/0/code.py:61:#     - No extra markers are added. The grid stays as a single clean binary motif recolored with 2 colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/21/code.py:44:#    - The layout keeps every-other-cell spacing, so multiple columns remain easy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/21/code.py:61:#      maximum count: bw = 2*K+1 and bh = key_row + 2*max_count + tail + slack.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D6/1/code.py:19:#     - The tail is no longer exactly two swatches. It now contains 3 or 4 swatches:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D6/1/code.py:26:#     - Output recolors each symbolic region with the matching swatch while keeping the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D6/1/code.py:118:def _recolor_symbolic_tile(symbolic_tile: np.ndarray, palette_colors: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D6/1/code.py:263:    - Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2 and repeat the recolored crop that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D6/1/code.py:289:    tile = _recolor_symbolic_tile(symbolic_tile, palette_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/