:    Recover the canonical template by undoing a repeated recolored strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D11/2/code.py:179:      the recoloring and border restoration become deterministic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:41:#      still the full 20x20 motif with only foreground/background recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:189:    - Use the border-colored cells to recover the rectangular in-bounds part of the crop, which reveals which sides of the 20x20 support were crossed and sharply narrows the allowed source offsets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D14/1/code.py:29:#      reduces ambiguity across multiple dihedral candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/5/code.py:27:#    - Keep 2-4 key colors and 1-5 external components per color so multiple legend columns remain visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/5/code.py:48:#    - In the output, at least one column extends upward for multiple dots, making the fused direction change legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/5/code.py:53:#    - No recoloring rule is introduced; colors remain direct identifiers linking outside sprites to legend entries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D5/1/code.py:50:#      visibly contains multiple colors after the move.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D5/1/code.py:56:#    - There is no hidden recoloring map. A token keeps its color when moved, which is directly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/0/code.py:39:#     - `min(counts)` was tied to a single minority pattern; with multiple singleton fragments that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/0/code.py:118:    assert len(counts) >= 3, \"need a majority pattern plus multiple anomaly fragments\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D1/2/code.py:31:# - If it were too large, multiple orientations/offsets could satisfy the visible cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/28/code.py:186:    - A connected black legend frame is divided by black separator lines into multiple rectangular cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D3/2/code.py:37:#   an exact recoloring of one binary motif window.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/13/code.py:28:#         with every dot recolored to one fixed tally color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:18:#    recolored teal (8) in the output. The maroon source cell itself still disappears to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:29:#      outside the destination. That is no longer enough; now we must also recolor every floor cell on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:34:#      In this variant wide open regions are harmful, because multiple shortest paths would make the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:47:#    Trails occupy narrow corridors outside the destination block and do not overlap the destination or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:48:#    walls. Multiple trails may share a trunk near the destination, which is visually coherent and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:162:    - Each chosen source maroon disappears back to orange, and every orange floor cell on its discovered route to the target is recolored teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/1/code.py:27:#   3. accent color -> paste an auxiliary recolored cell that shares the majority cell's shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/1/code.py:69:#   recolored majority-shape cells. Main-color pixels become copies of the full tricolor source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/1/code.py:161:    Enlarge a tricolor source cell into a 3x3 block of cell-sized copies and recolors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/1/code.py:167:      One of those patterns is a unique tricolor source cell; another is a recolored auxiliary cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/1/code.py:173:      and one color places the auxiliary recolored cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D9/1/code.py:52:#     - Each generated input includes reachable maroons at multiple frame depths, with at least one moved source beyond the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:31:#     - Keep the original spacing model intact: one turtle per arm tip, right-hand\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:34:#     - Change only the launch side. Vertical tips keep the original clockwise launch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:35:#       (initial heading = right of outward); horizontal tips launch from the mirrored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:41:#     - Original left tip:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:44:#     - Variant left tip:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:45:#       outward = west, initial heading = south, while the top/bottom tips still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:51:#       vertical tips behave one way, horizontal tips another way.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:61:#       side is mirrored for horizontal tips, those assumptions no longer hold.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:66:#     - The generator keeps the original size formula and minimum tip-to-border gap,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:212:    Grow four spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross, with launch direction tied to tip orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:218:    - Top and bottom tips launch from the clockwise side of their arm; left and right tips launch from the mirrored side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:223:    Key insight: The wall-following mechanics stay the same as the seed task, but flipping the launch side for the horizontal tips creates two endpoint-dependent winding families that visibly diverge from the uniform-clockwise baseline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:90:    - colors are unchanged from the seed task, so the new idea is isolated to destination multiplicity\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:181:    Route reachable maroon pixels into multiple 3×3 destination blocks around red centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:192:    Key insight: The task is no longer a single flood-fill. You must compare multiple BFS frontiers, decide ownership in overlapping reachable zones, and only then perform the row-major refill inside each separate container.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:200:    assert len(centers) >= 2, \"grid must contain multiple red centers for the multi-container variant\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/0/code.py:28:#    multiple grey sprites support each mapping. Dot layouts use only five fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/0/code.py:48:#    \"number of dots beside color X equals hole-count of grey sprites recolored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/0/code.py:221:CANVAS_SCALE = 1.2                  # sqrt(area) multiplier for canvas size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/22/code.py:22:#       2) some sprites are only 8-connected internally, so one visible sprite can split into multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/22/code.py:412:    - For each legend color, look only outside the box and count same-colored connected pieces using 4-connectivity, so diagonal-only contacts inside one sprite split into multiple counted parts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:23:#       the four arm tips define the smallest axis-aligned square frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:37:#       input tips lie on a 5x5 bbox around the center hole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:38:#       original logic would start four agents from those tips and connect\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:99:    \"\"\"List all fully in-bounds concentric frames starting from the tip bbox.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:143:    - Locate the cross center from the densest teal row/column, then read the four arm tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:144:    - The tips define the smallest rectangle; complete that perimeter, then expand the rectangle by 2 cells at a time.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D6/1/code.py:147:    Key insight: The original spiral can be discretized into its nested loop envelopes; once the tip-bbox is known, the whole output is just repeatedly padded rectangular frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D4/3/code.py:64:#      output recoloring rather than in extra clutter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:246:    - Ring boundaries are read from the same 1-cell-gap geometry as the seed task, so each extra ring starts 2 cells farther from the cross tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D10/1/code.py:47:#     grid: larger black canvas containing multiple separated rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D10/1/code.py:73:#     the solver can no longer terminate after a single local match; it must coordinate multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/3/code.py:13:#      itself has zero holes. The solver must sort legend blocks by row before recoloring sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/3/code.py:17:#      and may receive extras. Distractors remain present, so the task is not reduced to simple recolor-all.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/6/code.py:72:   - Legend width is sampled as `KEY_COLUMN + max_count + tail + slack`, guaranteeing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:12:#       - one black (0) plus-sign cross with a teal center hole marks the four launch tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:18:#       - original local step: a tip-adjacent black cell is empty, so the agent paints it teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:19:#       - variant local step: the corresponding tip-adjacent teal cell is untouched background, so the agent erases it to black\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:30:#     - generator still uses the original size formula and tip-to-border gap rule, so spirals have enough room\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:34:#     - from 2-3 examples a human can infer \"black paths are being cut out of a teal field from the black cross tips\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:41:#     - no conditional recoloring by rank/order is used\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:246:    Carve four clockwise spiral trenches from the tips of a black cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D14/0/code.py:252:    - Treat the black arms as the initial carved path and launch one turtle from each tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/0/code.py:27:#   and multiple wall styles, so the puzzle does not collapse to a trivial\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/2/code.py:22:#         - left cell = target recolor color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/2/code.py:33:#         - cells adjacent to hole interiors are recolored from grey to one marker color; outer mass stays grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/2/code.py:49:#       - one legend row can recolor sprites with different hole counts to the same output color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D5/2/code.py:52:#     - marker colors are few and repeated across multiple sprites, so the mapping can be inferred from 2-4 examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3