tion, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D3/3/code.py:277:    Grow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross, flipping path color at every 90-degree turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D3/3/code.py:283:    - Each arm tip launches a turtle whose initial heading is 90 degrees clockwise from the arm's outward direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D16/0/code.py:178:    - For every active stencil position, keep the underlying cell content but recolor only that cell's interior border as an overlay mark.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D5/1/code.py:99:        assert len(comps) >= 2, \"each non-frame color must arrive as multiple fragments\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:15:# Design analysis for the D11 recolor variant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:26:#   the same mask is located in the same way, but the scaled cells use a recolored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:36:# - The recolor rule has exactly one mapping case per sample:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:38:# - The generator rejects cases where the recolored template would match the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:62:# - The recolored output remains a clean single overlay on the same cell lattice;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:67:# - Because the recolored template uses the majority palette but a different pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:74:# - `main()` assumes the recolored template differs from the majority template so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:103:def _derive_recolored_pattern(minority_arr: np.ndarray, majority_arr: np.ndarray) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:104:    \"\"\"Return (mask, recolored_pattern) for the D11 transform.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/c