to that legend color; otherwise recolor it to a fixed marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/3/code.py:22:#      than isolated unrelated recolorings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/3/code.py:30:#    - The new solver must not read legend colors at all for recoloring, only for locating legend components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/3/code.py:51:#    - Legend colors are distinct and the gradient colors are distinct, so workspace recolorings are easy to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/3/code.py:159:    - If that hole count is listed by the legends, recolor the sprite with the fixed hole-count gradient;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/3/code.py:205:CANVAS_SCALE = 1.2                # sqrt(area) multiplier for canvas size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:21:#       - only existing ray tips launch spiral agents\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:29:#       - an L source with directions [U, R] launches only the top and right tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:34:#         which cardinal tips exist, and that subset controls the entire downstream fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:42:#       - both 2-tip and 3-tip cases are generated so the missing-launcher rule is repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:157:    Launch clockwise spiral walls only from the tips that exist in a teal T/L source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:164:    - Detect the black hub and keep only the cardinal tips that are actually present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:165:    - Each present tip launches a turtle heading 90° clockwise from its outward ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D5/2/code.py:107:    Fill the framed region with recolored sprite templates whose orientation depends on position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D5/2/code.py:117:    - Stamp that oriented sprite into the placeholder bbox, then recolor it using the legend mapping for that placeholder color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:18:#      enters a progressively narrower corridor and draws nested rectangular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:61:#      path's layer-by-layer penetration into a narrowing channel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:96:    - Once the path is painted, every blue pixel is recolored red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/0/code.py:20:#    different enclosed holes from their legend, yet they still recolor when the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/0/code.py:22:#    Example: a T-shaped legend with one hole can recolor a grey T-shaped sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/0/code.py:28:#    repeated matching sprites, so the shape-match rule is supported multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/0/code.py:32:#      multiple legends can share a hole count. The new lookup key is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/0/code.py:45:#    cavities but identical outlines recolor the same way.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/0/code.py:53:#    recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/5/code.py:37:#       - crop each grey component, count its holes, recolor by that lookup\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/5/code.py:41:#       - if exactly one legend color appears there, recolor to that color; otherwise erase\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/5/code.py:55:#       dependency: each sprite carries all information needed for recoloring inside its own mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/5/code.py:59:#       status_now: adapted; sprites with zero or multiple adjacent legend colors are erased\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/5/code.py:65:#     - matched sprites repeat legend colors at their edges, making the cause of recoloring local and visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/5/code.py:71:#     - only legend colors can trigger recoloring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/2/code.py:171:CANVAS_SCALE = 1.2                 # sqrt(area) multiplier for canvas size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D15/1/code.py:204:    - Turtles still launch from the four cross tips and still use the seed task's right-turn / straight / left candidate ordering with the same 2/1 step schedule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D3/0/code.py:13:#     output still draws one green orthogonal path to the opposite edge and recolors blue to red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D3/0/code.py:25:#     is the radius extraction inside the component loop; pathfinding, goal detection, and blue->red recoloring remain valid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D3/0/code.py:66:    - Once the route is drawn, all blue cells on the bars are recolored red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/4/code.py:15:    output: matched grey sprites recolor to the legend color; distractors erase to bg\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D1/4/code.py:52:    invalid because multiple legends intentionally share hole count 0. The replacement map is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D8/2/code.py:38:#   four quadrants. Therefore a human sees the same shape repeated in multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D8/2/code.py:40:#   Extra marker types prevent the task from collapsing into \"just recolor one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D9/2/code.py:20:#    - The original task builds one output frame crop containing every recolored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D9/2/code.py:30:#      that recolor-group are shown; other interior cells stay bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D9/2/code.py:38:#      avoids degenerate \"group by color\" cases where multiple legend entries\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D9/2/code.py:269:    Split the solved frame into multiple frame panels ordered by the visible legend entries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D9/2/code.py:277:    - Instead of drawing every recolored sprite into one output frame, build one frame panel per legend target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D9/2/code.py:278:    - In each panel, keep only the sprites whose legend recolors them to that panel's color, then concatenate the panels left-to-right in legend order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D9/2/code.py:280:    Key insight: The legend does double duty now: it still provides recoloring, and its spatial order determines how the separate output panels are arranged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:20:#   tip at the open end. The blue tip is the dangerous segment. Red cells remain solid obstacles, but only their\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:26:#   Variant: only the 3-cell blue tip emits the radius-3 halo; the path may run right next to the red body, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:27:#   swing wider only near the blue tip. The key difference is local danger at the tip instead of uniform danger\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:41:#   segment. The new generator must instead paint one contiguous blue tip so humans can see which bar region is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:44:#   prefer the first bar's red section; otherwise the start could land inside the hazardous tip and reduce the visual\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:45:#   contrast between safe-red hugging and blue-tip avoidance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:48:#   `a` and `b` are blue-tip lengths. This keeps their blue-tip halos from merging into an impossible wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:50:#   the hazardous tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:51:# - Blue tips are always on the open end, and every bar has at least `SAFE_RED_MIN` red cells so the safe segment is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:54:# - Across examples, people can compare red body vs blue tip directly: the path often slides beside red and only gives\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:58:# - The grid still contains only four colors and one object family. Blue is confined to tip segments, so overlays are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:62:#   are grouped into tip segments, humans can infer that blue is an annotation on part of the red obstacle rather than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:116:def _count_visible_danger_tips(inp: np.ndarray) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:117:    \"\"\"Count bars that visibly separate a blue danger tip from a red safe body.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:141:    Extend a green route from one border to the opposite, skimming red bar segments but steering wider around blue-marked danger tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:237:# Bar counts and blue-tip lengths\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:250:    \"\"\"Minimum main-axis size so blue-tip halos do not choke the corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:270:    \"\"\"Pick blue-tip lengths that fit the main-axis spacing constraints.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:280:    \"\"\"Valid bar length range given a blue tip and required open-side corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:297:    \"\"\"Paint a bar whose blue segment sits on the open tip, not on the wall side.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D20/1/code.py:403:    if _count_visible_danger_tips(inp) <= 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D1/1/code.py:46:#     - connector colors are fixed and visually repeated across multiple seams so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D2/0/code.py:35:#       is exercised multiple times instead of appearing only on rare samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D2/0/code.py:254:    - When the route is finished, recolor every blue pixel to red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D4/4/code.py:9:#   borrowed_idea: \"匹配成功后把对象内部改成背景色，核心动作是 erase 而不是 recolor\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D18/1/code.py:20:#      if the same bar is recolored blue, the path instead goes right to col 10. The color now changes the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D13/1/code.py:24:#       - every arm tip still launches the original clockwise spiral walker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D13/1/code.py:32:#     - In this variant, there are multiple center holes. The solver must instead\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D13/1/code.py:282:    - Detect every cross, sort the center holes in reading order, and start one agent from each arm tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D13/1/code.py:287:    - The local spiral rule is unchanged, but multiple visible source holes create a deterministic multi-source packing process where reading-order priority decides which spiral owns a contested corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D13/1/code.py:294:    \"\"\"Build a grid containing multiple plus-sign crosses with center holes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D18/2/code.py:25:#      3. Blue marker cells on each bar are recolored to that bar's base color, so the output bar is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D18/2/code.py:233:    Route a border-start path around keepout bars, recoloring each later segment from the most recently bypassed bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D1/1/code.py:117:#      appears in multiple orientations in the output, making the new rule directly inferable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D4/2/code.py:212:    - After the shortest low-turn route is found, background path cells near each bar are recolored by that bar's blue-count palette entry instead of all staying green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/0/code.py:21:#      key, and the glyph color is the recolor target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/0/code.py:26:#      zig-zag is valid and recolors all blue placements to red; a yellow boxed T-shape that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/0/code.py:51:#    - Humans can see that recoloring comes from boxed shape samples, not from placeholder\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/0/code.py:62:#      decoys while matched boxed shapes determine recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/0/code.py:281:    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them via boxed shape legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/0/code.py:293:    - Replace each placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the color of the matching legend box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/0/code.py:297:      Extra boxed glyphs are decoys and must be filtered out before recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/0/code.py:10:#     - Step 2 is replaced completely. The recolor legend no longer carries any\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/0/code.py:20:#       4. recolor to legend target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/0/code.py:26:#       5. recolor to that card's other color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/0/code.py:30:#       recolored to yellow even though red never appears in the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/0/code.py:50:#     - New recoloring assumes sprite areas are unique across source colors; the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/0/code.py:149:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and an area legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:18:#   by color match and recolor later.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:29:#     frame block color=3 -> find outside sprite color=3 -> stamp shape -> recolor via legend 3->7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:32:#     recolor sprite to 7 -> place it into every frame block colored 7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:33:# - This changes the causal dependency: placement now depends on the recolored result, not on the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:45:#   sprite lookup code must switch from color-keyed matching to shape-keyed recolor + target-keyed placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:55:# - Frame placeholders remain a clean grid with 1-cell gaps, making the recolor-then-place rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:104:    - Read each legend square to map sprite shape -> target color, then use that legend to logically recolor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:106:    - Place each recolored sprite into every same-target-color placeholder location inside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:109:    legend's shape match must be resolved first, and only the recolored result can be used to choose placement sites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:179:            assert tgt not in seen_targets, f\"multiple sprites matched target color {tgt}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:189:        f\"recolored sprite targets {sorted(target_to_sprite)} do not match placeholders {sorted(placeholder_colors)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:198:            f\"placeholder size does not match recolored sprite for target color {tgt_col}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D2/3/code.py:62:   - Because multiple samples vary bar lengths and blue counts, viewers can correlate larger blue counts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:24:#      but now it is essential: pass-through segments must stay red, so we must not recolor traversed red cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:181:def _solve_details(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict[str, object]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:219:    Key insight: Blue markers no longer decorate a universal obstacle type; they identify which bars repel the path, while unmarked red bars are traversable recoloring segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:221:    details = _solve_details(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:222:    out = np.array(details[\"grid\"], copy=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:223:    for r, c in details[\"path\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:387:        details = _solve_details(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:389:        if details[\"pass_bar_count\"] < 1 or details[\"detour_bar_count\"] < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D16/0/code.py:391:        if details[\"pass_bar_hits\"] < 1 or details[\"pass_cells\"] < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/1/code.py:35:      - final stamping previously asserted each placeholder color existed in color_map; now recolor defaults to source color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/1/code.py:113:    Fill the framed layout with sprite templates, recoloring only the colors that appear in the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D13/1/code.py:121:    - Stamp each template into every placeholder position; if that placeholder color has a legend entry, recolor the stamped sprite to the legend target color, otherwise leave it in its original color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/1/code.py:25:#      recolor to 7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/1/code.py:27:#      among legend tiles, find the tile whose ink mask is rot90(S) or flip(S) -> recolor to that tile's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/1/code.py:29:#      difference: source color no longer identifies the recolor target; only shape identity under transform\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/1/code.py:40:#    - Original recolor lookup used src color -> tgt color. That becomes src color -> sprite mask ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/1/code.py:55:#    - The output frame remains clean because only one recolored sprite is pasted per placeholder bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/1/code.py:271:    Fill the framed placeholders with matched sprites, then recolor them through a shape legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/1/code.py:285:    Key insight: Source color still chooses which shape to place, but final recoloring is keyed by shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:17:#   - The framed area, placeholder grid, sprite templates, and recoloring goal stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:32:#     frame, infer src/tgt directly from each local blob, then recolor sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:69:#     recolor bars appear on bottom/right edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:171:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using split edge legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:181:    - For each placeholder color, find the matching sprite template outside the frame, stamp it into each placeholder box, and recolor it using the reconstructed edge legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:183:    Key insight: No single legend fragment is complete by itself; the solver must aggregate boundary fragments from multiple edges, pair opposite spans into full legend entries, and then apply those mappings to the placed sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:24:#    - Output no longer recolors grey sprites in place. Every matching grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:25:#      sprite is removed from its old position, recolored by legend lookup, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:30:#      variant: the same blob is erased from (20,4), recolored to 7, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:36:#      a dense cluster near the legend instead of subtle local recolors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:43:#    - `out = g.copy()` + recolor grey cells in place is no longer valid because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/0/code.py:384:    - Matching sprites are recolored, removed from their original locations, and repacked beside the legend in hole-count order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:18:  recolored via the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:33:  frame may reuse one or more of its own colors multiple times. This keeps frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:42:  multiple frames, every frame bbox must be excluded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:98:    independently receives its matched recolored sprites\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:154:    Stamp recolored sprites into multiple framed regions using placeholder positions and a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:162:    - For each placeholder color, locate the matching-color sprite outside all frames and the legend that defines its recolor target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:163:    - Replace every placeholder occurrence inside its owning frame with the matched sprite shape recolored by the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:190:            assert col not in color_to_frame, f\"placeholder color {col} appears in multiple frames\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/3/code.py:103:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a position-coded legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/3/code.py:116:    Key insight: The recoloring key is no longer encoded by a special two-color shape; it is encoded spatially inside each 2x2 matrix, so the legend must be read column-wise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D16/2/code.py:27:#       otherwise many pieces would have valid placements in multiple rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:19:#   - A separate legend chooses the final recolor for each placed sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:23:#   - Replace step 2 completely: the recolor is no longer tied to source color or shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:41:#   - Old recolor logic at one placement: \"this sprite came from placeholder color 3, so find\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:43:#   - New recolor logic at the same placement: \"this sprite is being stamped into the frame's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:46:#   - Visible consequence: the same source color can appear in multiple regions and will then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:53:#     preventing accidental collapse back to a per-color recolor rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:56:#     That assumption is removed; recolor now depends on placeholder position, so the solver must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:71:#   - Output recolor differences can be seen immediately because the same source-colored placeholder\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py:138:    Stamp external sprites into the frame, then recolor them by a spatial legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:18:#     original: stamp the matching sprite into each placeholder box, then recolor every sprite pixel to legend tgt\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:19:#     new:      stamp the matching sprite, but recolor only the sprite's 4-neighbor boundary pixels to legend tgt;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:33:#     - recolor condition has exactly two classes (boundary/core), which is enough to be visible without introducing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:34:#       multiple hidden branches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:36:#       full recoloring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:39:#       the second-stage recoloring, not object detection\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:43:#       recoloring and must be replaced by a partial recolor renderer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:53:#       while the output repeatedly shows the same shape with only its outline recolored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:112:def _render_partial_recolor(mask: np.ndarray, src: int, tgt: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:113:    \"\"\"Render a sprite whose boundary pixels are recolored to tgt and whose core stays src.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:124:    Stamp matched sprites into the frame, then recolor only each sprite's outline using the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:284:        rendered = _render_partial_recolor(sprite_mask, src_col, tgt_col, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/0/code.py:475:        paste(output_frame, _render_partial_recolor(masks[src], src, color_to_tgt[src], bg), r0, c0, transparent=bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:31:#       - Every matched grey sprite is recolored to its legend color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:39:#       - Difference: topology-based recoloring still decides identity; D6 adds an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:40:#         explicit pairing visualization layer after recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:53:#       - The original recoloring loop assumes writing sprite colors in-place is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:63:#         recoloring does not overwrite unrelated objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:264:    - Count holes for every grey sprite; matching sprites are recolored to the corresponding legend color, while unmatched sprites are erased to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:265:    - After recoloring, draw a same-color straight connector from each matched sprite to the workspace-facing side of its legend patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/2/code.py:160:        assert len(uniq) <= 1, \"marker pixel participates in multiple diagonal pairs\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/2/code.py:19:#     - keep output = frame crop with placeholders replaced by recolored sprites\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/2/code.py:30:#     - under the old logic, recoloring depended on finding a shape/color pair legend;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/2/code.py:128:    Replace frame placeholders with counted sprites and recolor them using a top-left count legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/2/code.py:139:    Key insight: The legend no longer identifies shapes at all; its nested dot counts are the lookup key, so sprite area determines the recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:55:#      the compact two-color legend selects the recolor target. The new difficulty is spatial,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:117:    Stamp recolored sprites into an irregular framed region using placeholder anchors and a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:121:    - Outside the frame bbox: sprite shapes (one per placeholder color) and compact two-color legends that specify recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/2/code.py:89:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a color lookup table.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/2/code.py:101:    Key insight: The sprite still comes from the placeholder color, but recoloring no longer depends on a secondary shape clue; the upper-left legend is now a direct color-to-color dictionary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/1/code.py:53:#       using exactly two colors. This is more informative than a flat recolor but still learnable from 2-4 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/1/code.py:54:#     - Each source color appears in multiple placeholder slots whenever possible, so the same patterned recoloring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D6/1/code.py:79:#       monochrome recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/0/code.py:26:#    - To keep the hierarchy visible, every non-background color appears multiple times in the input,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/4/code.py:64:   - Because direction sets vary but output depends only on arm count, multiple markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D15/2/code.py:274:    - The template's bounding box gives the target output height and width, but carries no color detail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:18:#   the frame. The same placeholder color can therefore recolor differently on the two sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:23:#   source is still global by color, but recoloring is now (region, color) dependent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:48:#   by color id is used to decide the recoloring; side membership comes only from visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:56:#   That keeps recoloring structural and local: same placeholder color + same sprite shape, but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:297:    Stamp recolored sprites into a partitioned frame using placeholder positions and side-local legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:309:    - Shape selection is still global by placeholder color, but recoloring is regional: the left legends control left-chamber placements and the right legends control right-chamber placements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/3/code.py:29:#       output pastes M at each color-2 placeholder and recolors it to 7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/3/code.py:32:#       but the pasted shape is rot90(M, clockwise) recolored to 7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/3/code.py:33:#       if the frame is green, the pasted shape stays M recolored to 7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/3/code.py:35:#       the matching and recoloring pipeline is unchanged; only the frame color injects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/3/code.py:114:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region, with the frame color controlling sprite orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/3/code.py:122:    - Use placeholder color to pick the matching outside sprite and use the legend to pick the final recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/3/code.py:126:    - The outside legend still explains only the recoloring, while the frame color itself explains the orientation change, so solving the task requires combining both cues.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:149:      that hole count are recolored; light-grey sprites with the same hole count are erased.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/0/code.py:150:    - If a legend hole count has no dark-grey sprite, matching light-grey sprites are recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/0/code.py:25:#     - Output keeps only the frame crop and recolors each stamped sprite to the legend target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/0/code.py:28:#       -> solver pastes that sprite and recolors it by the blue legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/0/code.py:33:#     - Source types remain 2-5, and each type can repeat across multiple slots, so shape matching is exercised repeatedly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/0/code.py:52:#     - The recoloring rule remains exposed by the unchanged legend mechanism, so only one reasoning step changes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/0/code.py:55:#     - Interior regions contain one sparse marker per occupied slot, which is visually cleaner than mixing multiple overlays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/0/code.py:106:    - Outside the frame: one sprite template per source color plus a compact two-color legend for the final recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/1/code.py:44:#       colors and multiple anchors so the solver is not forced to infer many unrelated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/1/code.py:77:#     color id is used. The legend still gives explicit recoloring evidence, while the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/1/code.py:140:    Rebuild a framed sprite mosaic from single-pixel anchors, then recolor it with the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/1/code.py:147:    - Detect the frame, its in-frame anchor colors, the matching external sprites, and the legend-based recoloring map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/1/code.py:153:    The legend still controls recoloring, but D14 changes placement: the anchor is no longer a whole placeholder block. Its absolute position inside the frame tells you which sprite corner should lock onto it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/4/code.py:90:    Fill the frame with recolored sprites, choosing each shape by complementary color instead of same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/4/code.py:99:    - Stamp that sprite into every placeholder bbox, then recolor the stamped pixels to the legend target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/4/code.py:101:    Key insight: The legend still controls the final recoloring, but shape lookup is no longer same-color matching; examples establish a small color-swap system where blue<->red, green<->yellow, and pink<->orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/2/code.py:17:#     - After placement, the full sprite footprint, including the anchor cell, is recolored to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/2/code.py:56:#       changes where the sprite lands, not how recoloring is decided.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/2/code.py:104:    Place recolored sprites into a framed region by matching anchor-marked templates to target pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/2/code.py:119:    sprite acts as an anchor, and the legend still provides the final recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/2/code.py:329:    \"\"\"Render the final recolored sprite footprint.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/1/code.py:20:#    pre-swap board -> recolor each mirror-signature family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/1/code.py:274:        assert len(cols) == len(groups), \"slot multiplicity must match input multiplicity\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/1/code.py:299:    - After the pre-swap rectangle is reconstructed, recolor every non-frame slot with the color of its left-right mirrored partner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:28:#   read cell (3,2) -> recolor the whole border to that color -> return the recolored grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:50:#   colors; this remains safe because recoloring happens strictly after assembly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:53:#   The new code must route every solved board through the border recolor step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:85:#   supporting human induction of the post-assembly recoloring rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:233:def _apply_border_recolor(board: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:342:    return _apply_border_recolor(base).astype(int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:503:    real_final = _apply_border_recolor(real_base)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:612:    transformed = _apply_border_recolor(base)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D11/3/code.py:632:    if np.array_equal(got, _apply_border_recolor(base)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/1/code.py:88:    Stamp recolored sprites into a marked frame using edge-color coordinates and a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:27:#    - Follower sprites intentionally use hole counts outside the legend set, so their recoloring cannot be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:29:#    - The generator guarantees multiple propagation edges per sample so the new logic is repeated, not anecdotal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:34:#      In the variant, erasing too early would destroy components that should be recolored in later rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:43:#    - The new rule is visible because some recolored sprites have the \"wrong\" hole count for every legend entry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:56:#      but are recolored via propagation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:180:    - First recolor every grey component whose own hole count appears in the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:181:    - Then repeatedly recolor any still-grey component that touches already recolored components by 8-neighborhood;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D11/2/code.py:182:      if all recolored neighbors agree on one color, the untouched component inherits that color. Components that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/2/code.py:14:#        source color to determine the final recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/2/code.py:28:#      - Both are replaced: `main()` now indexes sprites by bbox dims, and the generator creates multiple sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/2/code.py:33:#      - Same-sized holes appear multiple times; the same outside sprite shape reappears in those holes after recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/2/code.py:40:#        target color, the recoloring cue stays structured and learnable while the size cue controls shape choice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/2/code.py:86:    Fill a framed layout with recolored sprites chosen by placeholder size rather than sprite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/2/code.py:97:    - Stamp that sprite into every same-color placeholder location, then recolor the stamped pixels using the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/2/code.py:100:    recoloring. The sprite identity is determined by measuring bbox dimensions and matching those sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D3/3/code.py:52:#     - No color-id-based ordering or recoloring rule is used. The template color is simply preserved as-is.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:27:#   recoloring is still driven by the source-color legend, not by the connector.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:31:#     use legend red->yellow to recolor the stamped shape yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:36:#     legend red->yellow to recolor the stamped shape yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:38:#     the source color still controls recoloring, but no longer controls shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:44:#   * at least one connector color is shared by multiple sprite types\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:45:#   * at least one connector shape is shared by multiple sprite types\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:203:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using connector-marked placeholders and a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:208:      with their own connectors, plus the same small color legend used for output recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:213:    - Stamp only the sprite body into the placeholder position, then recolor that stamped body using the legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D1/3/code.py:217:    key, while the original legend still supplies the final recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/3/code.py:18:#     variant: assemble the hidden rectangle exactly as before, then recolor each finished\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/3/code.py:30:#     a per-cell stripe recolor would erase all jigsaw boundaries and reduce the task to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/3/code.py:32:#     mechanism. Piece-level recolor preserves the need to reconstruct the hidden packing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/3/code.py:38:#       into source-color components -> recolor each recovered piece by its horizontal zone.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/3/code.py:45:#     hidden source pieces exclude {1,2,3}; therefore every produced answer is genuinely recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8