l provides the only source->target recoloring cue. Because accent colors are not part of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D3/0/code.py:252:    - Paste the entire two-color sprite into each matching placeholder position, then recolor only the primary-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D3/0/code.py:255:    Key insight: The legend still controls recoloring, but shape retrieval now depends on isolating a multicolor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D3/0/code.py:385:def _recolor_primary(patch: np.ndarray, primary: int, target: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D3/0/code.py:499:        paste(output_frame, _recolor_primary(sprites[src], src, tgt_cols[src]), r0, c0, transparent=bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:21:#     source sprite color -> final recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:26:#     A sprite is selected by exact bbox size, then recolored via the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:29:#     can repeat across multiple cavities, so the size clue is repeated within a sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:35:#     bbox is 3x4, then use that source color's legend pair to recolor the placed piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:61:#     and external sprites correspond by dimensions, while legends still explain recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:124:    Fill framed cavities with size-matched sprites, then recolor them using the outside legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:136:      that sprite into the cavity, and recolor it with the legend's output color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/0/code.py:139:    a jigsaw slot, so bbox size identifies the source sprite and the legend only controls recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:9:#   The variant changes only the output stage: matched sprites are recolored, tight-cropped,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:23:#   depends only on matched objects. The old per-cell recolor loop is replaced by component\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:31:#   Across examples, humans can see that only legend-matching sprites survive, get recolored by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:114:    \"\"\"Extract matched grey sprites as recolored tight patches plus their scene bboxes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:189:    - Keep only sprites whose hole count appears in the legend, recolor each one to the mapped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:234:CANVAS_SCALE = 1.2                 # sqrt(area) multiplier for canvas size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/1/code.py:45:#     - `out[mask] = 8` still matches the original hollow-body recolor rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/1/code.py:116:    - If a component contains enclosed cavities, recolor that component itself to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D15/0/code.py:153:    - If a component encloses holes, recolor the component to teal (8) and those holes to magenta (6).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/2/code.py:14:#     - then recolor every cell that 4-touches a differently colored assembled neighbor to a fixed seam color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/2/code.py:15:#     - only interior piece-to-piece contacts count; the outside border alone does not trigger recoloring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/2/code.py:48:#   - _build_requirements() still writes original colors into req. This is correct because seam recoloring happens\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D6/2/code.py:282:      frame anchors, then apply the seam recoloring as a deterministic postprocess derived from local adjacencies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:225:    Add red outlines around objects, and also treat deep narrow indentations as holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:229:    - Some objects have true enclosed holes; others may instead have a narrow deep notch that opens to the outside from one side of the object's tight bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:233:    - If a component has either enclosed holes or deep narrow boundary indentations, recolor the component to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:237:    - The output is computed from a \"filled\" version of each component: classical closed holes and qualifying deep indentations both become part of the solid mask used for recoloring and outlining, while shallow or wide concavities remain ordinary background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:19:#      legend still maps src -> tgt for the final recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:23:#        external 3x4 legend says 7 over 4  => sprite 7 is finally recolored to 4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:33:#    - Placeholder color helps identify the src side of the external recolor legend: no longer safe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:46:#    - The lookup legend sits alone in the top-left, while sprite templates and recolor legends remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:50:#      original overlapping legend. Both are repeated across multiple placements and colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:56:#    - Every src also has exactly one overlapping recolor legend block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:155:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region after decoding placeholder colors through a lookup legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:159:    - Outside the frame: source-color sprite templates, the original overlapping recolor legends, and a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:165:    - Use src to locate the outside sprite shape, then use the original overlapping legend to recolor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:169:    top-left lookup legend must be read first, and only then can the old src-to-tgt recolor legend apply.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:269:        f\"recolor legends {sorted(color_map)} do not match sprite colors {sorted(mapped_sources)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:17:#      The outside legend still recolors red's sprite after placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:37:#    - Markers are single cells placed in narrow bands above and left of the frame, aligned to valid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:40:#      narrow dedicated bands above and left of the frame; only their alignment, not their distance from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:60:#      legend outside the frame. The legend is still the only cue for output recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:126:    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using edge-projected coordinates and a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:130:    - Just outside the frame: colored row markers in a narrow band left of the frame and column markers in a narrow band above it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:136:    - Locate the matching outside sprite, stamp it at each inferred destination, and recolor it using the outside legend mapping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/1/code.py:138:    Key insight: The frame interior gives no placement hints anymore — position is reconstructed from colored edge projections, while the legends still provide the final recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D4/1/code.py:12:#         an