u/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D13/0/code.py:62:#    special hollow-object recoloring, so the variant is easier to infer than the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D13/0/code.py:234:    Decode an edge legend, then recolor and outline the real blue objects accordingly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D13/0/code.py:245:    - For each real object outside the legend, recolor solid ones with the legend's solid fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D13/0/code.py:246:    - If an object encloses a background hole, recolor its shell and hole with the legend's hollow colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D13/0/code.py:249:    Key insight: The geometric transformation is still \"detect holes, optionally recolor, then outline\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D11/2/code.py:130:    Use the largest object as a reference, then recolor nearby objects before outlining.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D11/2/code.py:138:    - Find the largest component and recolor it, plus every component within Chebyshev distance 4 of it, to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D7/3/code.py:107:    Process each object in three linked stages: classify holes, recolor interiors, then choose an outline style.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D7/3/code.py:115:    - If holes are present, recolor the object to teal (8), recolor the holes to magenta (6), and draw a full red (2) 8-neighborhood outline around the object-plus-holes mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D7/3/code.py:119:    - The hole test now controls two later actions: hollow objects get interior recoloring and a solid outline, while solid objects skip recoloring and receive a dotted outline chosen from the same outer ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D13/2/code.py:164:    - If a main component encloses holes, recolor the component teal and those holes magenta before outlining, treating the holes as filled for the outline calculation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D13/2/code.py:166:    Key insight: The pre-outlined corner sample is instructional rather than transformable; it explicitly encodes the border neighborhood/width, while the hollow-object recoloring rule stays the same as in the original task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:21:#    - Hollow objects are still recolored teal, but each enclosed hole is filled independently:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:24:#      original logic: detect a hollow component -> recolor all its fg cells to 8 -> fill every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:26:#      new logic: detect the same holes -> recolor fg cells to 8 -> for each hole compute\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:61:#      size bands in a grid, usually with one object containing multiple holes of different sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:63:#      accidental object-specific recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:66:#    - Holes are rectangular and separated by at least one fg corridor, so multiple markings inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D5/2/code.py:152:    - A component that contains enclosed holes is recolored teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D14/0/code.py:28:#   - Only five visible semantic colors are used, and each appears on multiple pieces across the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D6/0/code.py:120:    - If a component encloses holes, recolor the component to teal and the enclosed holes to magenta before outlining.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D6/0/code.py:122:    Key insight: The object-wise recoloring and outlining rule is unchanged; the only new step is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D12/2/code.py:50:#       every sample still contains multiple solid and hollow objects, giving repeated evidence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D12/2/code.py:52:#     - old `out[mask] = 8` assumed hollow recolor is globally fixed; now it must use the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D12/2/code.py:229:    Use an edge legend to decide how objects, holes, and outlines should be recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D12/2/code.py:236:    - Read the legend as: object->outline, object->hollow-object recolor, hollow-object recolor->hole-fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D12/2/code.py:238:    - If an object encloses background holes, recolor the object body with the decoded hollow color, fill its holes with the decoded hole color, then compute the outline around that solidified mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D16/1/code.py:19:#    - Output keeps the original interior recolor rule for hollow objects:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D16/1/code.py:37:#    - `if holes:` still safely means \"apply teal/magenta recolor\", because that rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D16/1/code.py:43:#      shared one color. With multiple colors it would be wrong if rings from different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D16/1/code.py:131:    - If a component contains enclosed holes, recolor the object teal (8), recolor each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:33:#       narrow: width == 1, stays blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:34:#       wide: width >= 2, recolored teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:38:#     - recolor only wide frames to teal (8); narrow frames remain blue (1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:42:#     \"has any interior hole?\" -> yes -> recolor full object teal, fill hole magenta, outline the hole-filled mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:45:#     if hole bbox implies thickness 2 -> recolor frame teal, fill hole magenta, outline outer rectangle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:50:#   - Every sample contains both narrow and wide frames, so the blue/teal split is observable in 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:56:#     That becomes wrong here because all frames have holes but narrow ones must stay blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:145:    - Recolor only wide frames (thickness >= 2) to teal (8); narrow one-pixel frames stay blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:242:    num_narrow = random.randint(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[0], min(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[1], num_components - 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:248:    thicknesses = [NARROW_THICKNESS] * num_narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:249:    thicknesses.extend(random.choice(wide_choices) for _ in range(num_components - num_narrow))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D17/1/code.py:24:#       2. the old scattered locations, recolored grey, showing where pieces came from.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D17/1/code.py:279:    - Pieces that were already part of the frame stay there; every other source cell is recolored grey to show the fragment's origin.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D4/0/code.py:23:#       recolor component body to teal (8)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D4/0/code.py:24:#       recolor enclosed hole cells to magenta (6)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D4/0/code.py:122:    - If the component contains enclosed holes, recolor its body to teal (8), recolor each hole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D4/0/code.py:128:      interior recoloring, and hollow objects must be outlined as if their holes were filled in.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D6/1/code.py:126:    Add red outlines around objects, recolor hollow ones, then crop away empty border area.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D6/1/code.py:134:    - If a component encloses holes, recolor that component to teal (8) and recolor each enclosed hole to magenta (6).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D6/1/code.py:135:    - After all recoloring and outlining is complete, crop the result to the smallest rectangle containing every non-background result pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D4/1/code.py:29:#    red/orange/yellow respectively while preserving the same hollow recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D4/1/code.py:47:#    Outline colors are limited to red/orange/yellow/green, while interior recolors remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D4/1/code.py:123:    - If a component has enclosed holes, recolor its body to teal (8) and those holes to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/0/code.py:17:#     original: any object with >=1 enclosed hole used one fixed recolor pair (body=8, holes=6)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/0/code.py:25:#     Example: a ring with two disconnected rectangular voids was previously recolored the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/0/code.py:27:#     first be recognized as having exactly two interior background components, then recolored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/0/code.py:39:#     - the original unconditional recolor `out[mask] = 8` depended on every hollow object\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/0/code.py:122:    Add red outlines around objects, and recolor hollow objects by the number of enclosed holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/0/code.py:132:    - Hollow components are recolored before outlining according to their hole count:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/1/code.py:19:#     hollow_rule: only hollow components are recolored, and the shell color depends on the component's input color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/1/code.py:27:#     ensure one source color appears in both a hollow object and a solid object, proving the recolor depends on hole-status plus source color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/1/code.py:35:#     this preserves the original non-overlap guarantee for red outlines even after recoloring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/1/code.py:98:    - Objects can use multiple source colors, and some of them enclose 4-connected background holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/1/code.py:103:    - Hollow objects recolor their shell by a fixed source-color mapping, fill enclosed holes with magenta (6), then receive the same red outline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D16/2/code.py:33:#      That assumption no longer holds, so the area check must happen before recoloring or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D16/2/code.py:45:#      from just a few examples instead of blending into the old hole-based recoloring rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/1/code.py:34:#     - original logic: a 1x3 hole and a 2x2 hole both trigger the same recolor, shell=8 and hole=6\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/1/code.py:45:#   - _interior_holes computes holes from the original blue mask, not from recolored output; still valid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/1/code.py:125:    Add red outer outlines around components, while recoloring hollow ones by hole size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/1/code.py:133:    - If a component has enclosed holes, sum all enclosed hole cells before recoloring it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/1/code.py:136:    Key insight: The outline still treats holes as filled-in mass, but the interior recolor is no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/2/code.py:131:    - A green-adjacent component is processed with the hollow branch: recolor the blue cells to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/2/code.py:132:      teal (8), recolor any enclosed background holes to magenta (6), and treat those holes as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/2/code.py:27:#      original logic first recolors the shell to teal and the hole to magenta, then computes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/2/code.py:127:    - For every foreground component, recolor its boundary cells red (2) on the object side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/2/code.py:130:    - If a component encloses holes, recolor the component to teal (8) and those holes to magenta (6)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D8/0/code.py:166:    Add red outlines around objects, and recolor hollow ones by the geometry of their holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:13:#      are still recolored magenta before outlining.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:14:#    - The only semantic flip is which objects get recolored teal:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:18:#        * a solid 3x3 block: original output keeps it blue; variant recolors the whole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:20:#        * a hollow ring with a 2x2 hole: original recolors ring teal and hole magenta;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:21:#          variant keeps ring blue, recolors only the hole magenta, then draws the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:40:#      stay blue, so the hole branch must avoid recoloring the object body and only recolor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D2/2/code.py:125:    - If a component has no enclosed background holes, recolor the component to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/4/code.py:193:    - If a component encloses holes, recolor the component to teal (8) and those holes to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/3/code.py:27:#     - For nested objects, recolor only the outer blue shell to teal, keep the green inner object\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/3/code.py:64:#     keep that core while recoloring only the shell. This is a direct visual contrast with solid objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/3/code.py:155:    - If a blue component encloses another colored object, recolor only the blue shell to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D3/3/code.py:158:    Key insight: The shell geometry still defines the enclosed pocket, but the pocket is no longer a hole to fill; it is an existing inner object that must be preserved while the shell is recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/1/code.py:18:#     - Keep the original hollow-object recoloring rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/1/code.py:31:#     - Large components are capped to moderate areas so multiple radius-3 halos still fit on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/1/code.py:108:    Draw size-dependent red halos around objects, while preserving the original hole recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/1/code.py:117:    - Hollow objects are recolored teal (8), and their enclosed holes are recolored magenta (6).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/3/code.py:30:#   Only D1 changes. Object colors, hole handling, hole recoloring, and 8-neighbor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/3/code.py:113:    - If a component encloses holes, recolor the component teal (8), recolor those\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/0/code.py:26:#     - 1-2 components are hollow and still trigger teal(8) shell + magenta(6) hole recoloring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/0/code.py:46:#     - recoloring before outlining remains safe because the outline is still written only onto\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/0/code.py:62:#       pile-up from mixing multiple marking systems in the same local region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/0/code.py:152:    - If a component encloses holes, recolor its body to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D8/