ties appear multiple times.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D3/2/code.py:53:      and more local detail, so flood-fill is the only robust way to recover the partition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D3/2/code.py:348:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D3/0/code.py:85:            raise AssertionError(\"Non-hub branch node has multiple forward neighbors\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/8/code.py:47:# - The old \"arm-tip nozzle span\" checks no longer make sense. The new solver replaces them\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/8/code.py:53:# - Because one frame now owns multiple markers, the solver must keep all adjacent component ids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/8/code.py:294:    Key insight: the frame side is the directional cue, and one frame can contribute multiple independent rays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/0/code.py:51:# - The grid is large enough for multiple stripe steps: generator uses sizes 24+.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D14/2/code.py:93:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/6/code.py:22:#    generator therefore enforces three run-length buckets (short / medium / long) and multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/6/code.py:24:#    bucket can be realized by multiple input colors, so the answer cannot be a simple per-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/10/code.py:42:#      split an edge-hugging orange band into multiple components. The rule never required one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D12/1/code.py:42:#    - Removing ambiguous straight walls prevents collisions between multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/20/code.py:39:#    legend is supported by multiple copies rather than a single accidental pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D13/2/code.py:25:#    - The solver still supports all original collision branches. The generator narrows the placement space to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/1/code.py:29:#    stripe's current narrowed span. Green stripes still recolor the entire row/column's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/1/code.py:30:#    existing non-background pixels to green before repainting the narrowed stripe cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/1/code.py:48:#    Samples are rejected unless the produced output shows multiple distinct stripe widths\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/1/code.py:49:#    and at least one green flood changes a foreground pixel outside the narrowed stripe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D15/0/code.py:32:#     - A block color now appears on multiple 3x3 motifs instead of exactly one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D15/0/code.py:141:    - Elsewhere, each block color appears on multiple small same-colored motif sprites; their positions encode order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:19:#    a boundary / arm-tip color. Second, the marker is no longer a tiny strip: it is a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:23:#    the ray axis. Example: if a 3x2 seed touches the right tip color of a plus, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:30:#    This makes the combo visually distinct from the original narrow markers without\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:38:#      combo the marker is attached specifically to the tip-color boundary cells, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:61:#    changes appearance rather than being a hidden parity detail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:72:#    the shared tip color, the seed bbox is a full rectangular period whose cross span\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:146:def detect_tip_color(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:295:    - Each anchor is a repeated two-color plus-like sprite: an interior color and a boundary / tip color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:301:      components, then identify which of those two colors is the shared tip color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:302:    - For each non-plus component touching that tip color, infer the launch direction from the attachment\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:309:      solver must read the anchor as a composite two-color object, use the tip-color adjacency to identify\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:326:    tip_color = detect_tip_color(g, plus_lab, int(pn), plus_pair)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:327:    if tip_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:340:        tip_mask = plus_mask & (g == int(tip_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:342:        for r, c in np.argwhere(tip_mask):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:364:                    if 0 <= rr < H and 0 <= cc < W and bool(tip_mask[rr, cc]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:432:    0 = empty, 1 = core color, 2 = boundary / arm-tip color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:630:    tip_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:684:                out[r, c] = int(core_color if role == 1 else tip_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:739:    core_color, tip_color = map(int, rng.choice(others, size=2, replace=False))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:740:    palette = [c for c in others if c not in {core_color, tip_color}]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:763:            tip_color=tip_color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:70:#      hub-to-tip. The output groups colors by branch order, so both the tree topology and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:79:#      branch to be reversed relative to hub-to-tip geometry so the color cue is genuinely needed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:125:            raise ValueError(\"Non-hub branch node has multiple forward neighbors\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:172:def _choose_branch_read(colors_hub_to_tip: list[int], palette: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:173:    reverse = list(reversed(colors_hub_to_tip))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:174:    forward_score = _cycle_mismatch_count(colors_hub_to_tip, palette)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:178:    return colors_hub_to_tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:200:    - For each branch, compare hub->tip against tip->hub and keep the direction whose colors best\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:318:        colors_hub_to_tip = [int(grid[r, c]) for r, c in cells]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:319:        expected.extend(_choose_branch_read(colors_hub_to_tip, palette))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:335:        colors_hub_to_tip = [int(grid[r, c]) for r, c in cells]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/30/code.py:336:        chosen = _choose_branch_read(colors_hub_to_tip, palette)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D6/1/code.py:246:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D4/1/code.py:413:    - when there are multiple cues, both cue orientations appear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:140:def _ray_region_details(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:200:    region, _, _, _ = _ray_region_details(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:289:    reach, _, _, _ = _ray_region_details(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:437:    _, horizontal_seed, vertical_seed, _ = _ray_region_details(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:445:    vert_tail = np.full((h, w), -1, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:446:    horiz_tail = np.full((h, w), -1, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:452:                vert_tail[r, c] = max(vert_tail[r, c], len(cells) - i - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:458:                horiz_tail[r, c] = max(horiz_tail[r, c], len(cells) - i - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:471:    candidate = interior & (vert_tail >= 0) & (horiz_tail >= 0) & ((vert_tail >= 2) | (horiz_tail >= 2))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/33/code.py:515:    \"\"\"Return the inclusive cross-axis span of one arm tip.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D6/0/code.py:24:#    steps and multiple turns. At the same time, it avoids extra self-touching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D6/0/code.py:43:#    Each generated sample contains multiple diagonal edges, so more than 10% of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D6/2/code.py:290:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:52:# - There are no multiple objects, so overlap constraints are unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D11/0/code.py:35:#    changes multiple previously painted rows/cols. Generator rejection also enforces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/12/code.py:187:    - Foreground may contain detached 2-3 pixel noise blobs in the same two c