/code.py:758:                \"tail_len\": int(tail_len),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/78332cb0/D3/2/code.py:206:    raise AssertionError(\"ambiguous: multiple chains found in the same orientation\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D5/3/code.py:40:#    - Marker colors still repeat across multiple sprites sometimes, preserving the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D6/0/code.py:317:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D11/2/code.py:543:        tail_cells = _trace_to_edge(last_start, tuple(placed[-1][\"out_dir\"]), n)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D11/2/code.py:544:        if len(tail_cells) - 1 < MIN_TAIL_CELLS:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D11/2/code.py:546:        for j, cell in enumerate(tail_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D11/2/code.py:557:        used_cells.update(tail_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D3/2/code.py:168:            f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) has multiple aligned companions: {aligned}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:37:#    - The core change is region multiplicity, not new glyph logic. Keeping the glyph set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:43:#    - `len(colors_present(...)) == 1`: no longer valid; now multiple distinct foreground\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:45:#    - Global bbox extraction of all foreground pixels would wrongly merge multiple glyphs;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头形精灵凸出方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:15:# - This combo replaces the source object with arrow-shaped anchors and simultaneously changes the direction cue:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:16:#   the ray must follow the arrow's protruding head, not the side where the seed happens to touch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:18:#   Example: a right-facing arrow may have its seed above or below it, but the output still repeats that seed to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:22:# - Arrow templates are limited to a few reusable families so humans can learn \"the protruding tip points the ray\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:24:# - Each grid uses at least two arrow orientations, so the shape cue is actually demonstrated inside one sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:26:# - `detect_dominant_big_component_color()` still works because arrows remain the only components with bbox >= 3x3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:31:# - The generator is output-first: place full arrows and full rays first, then erase all but one long clue ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:32:# - Arrows, rays, and their 4-neighborhood guards are kept separate so two non-arrow components never merge under\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:33:#   `label_mask((grid != bg) & (grid != arrow_color))`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:34:# - Candidate seeds are rejected if they go out of bounds, overlap, or even touch previously committed rays / arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:36:# - The crucial cue is human-visible geometry: each arrow has one protruding tip and that tip points the repetition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:38:# - The kept pre-extended clue ray shows that the repeated payload follows the arrow orientation rather than contact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:41:# - No ray is allowed to touch a foreign arrow or another ray, so each object stays visually isolated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:44:# - No ordering on color ids is used. Colors only separate background / arrow anchors / payload tiles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:47:# - For every generated arrow, the attachment side should be orthogonal to the true ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:50:# - Solver assumes each big anchor component exactly matches one rotated arrow template below.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:51:# - Solver assumes each arrow has exactly one adjacent non-arrow component (seed or pre-extended ray component).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:215:def _build_arrow_lookup() -> dict[tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:224:_ARROW_LOOKUP = _build_arrow_lookup()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:227:def _match_arrow_direction(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:254:def detect_arrow_component_color(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:260:    \"\"\"Choose the color whose big components best match the arrow template family.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:283:            if _match_arrow_direction(local) is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:295:# Extend marker rays from arrow-shaped anchors using the arrow head as the only direction cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:298:# - One dominant non-background color forms several arrow sprites, all drawn from the same small template family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:299:# - Each arrow touches exactly one colored marker component, and exactly one of those components may already be a long\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:302:# - Recognize the arrow's facing direction from its protruding tip, not from the marker's contact side.\n/