f/D12/0/code.py:66:#     intentionally touches multiple different line colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/23/code.py:48:#    - A new potential conflict appears when multiple motifs overlap with opposite roles. The generator avoids this by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/23/code.py:469:    \"\"\"Return feasible matching-motif multiplicities for the sampled block count.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/14/code.py:46:#     one seed touches multiple branches; each branch can map to a different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/14/code.py:49:#     there is still one seed with multiple branches, but the branches now share\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/14/code.py:60:#   - Branch count is fixed at 2 so the \"single seed, multiple same-color starts\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/14/code.py:69:#   - \"one seed -> one line start\" is no longer valid; the seed must have multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/14/code.py:88:#     plus one line color that visibly expands into multiple cavities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/14/code.py:189:    Fill every frame cavity reachable from a single border seed that fans into multiple same-color branches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/14/code.py:194:    - That seed touches multiple 4-neighbor line starts, and all of those branches share one line color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/1/code.py:26:#     - body: 4-13 pixels of one color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/1/code.py:62:#   - anchor colors are unique per anchor; multiple sprites may share the same marker_A color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D18/2/code.py:54:#      multiple beam colors in the same corridor would make the output visually messy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D13/0/code.py:34:#   - The geometry is kept to one family of adjacent basins with a narrow transfer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/0/code.py:50:#     - Only two interior regions are used (orange head-side slab, grey tail slab),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/0/code.py:53:#     - Multiple containers still appear, with both distance-capped and fuel-capped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D4/1/code.py:132:    - Each seed is a unique-color 2-3 pixel block lying on the outer border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/6/code.py:69:#      that multiple same-colored motifs all matter to the carved result.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:21:#      thick L mask, with 2-cell red ports only at branch tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:22:#    - A tip port now encodes two facts at once: it marks that this branch exists\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:24:#      Example: if the anchor has a red tip on its top branch, the directly docked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:28:#      the anchor is stricter: the whole 2-cell tip must be covered by the child\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:32:#      exposes a small subset of branch tips. This keeps the new rule visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:33:#    - Cross anchors use exactly 3 of 4 tips; L anchors use both exposed tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:41:#      tip reds are now grouped by side, and a legal direct attachment must cover\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:42:#      both red cells of that tip with a piece port on the opposite side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:49:#    - Anchor ports are represented explicitly, because L anchors have branch tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:53:#    - The yellow anchor geometry is directly visible, and the red tip locations\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:60:#    - The anchor remains monochrome yellow except at active red tip cells, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:69:#      half of an anchor tip. Generated samples require this metric to be >= 1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:72:#      and that each red tip side is either fully active (2 red cells) or inactive.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:74:#    - `main()` assumes the direct anchor child for each active tip uses the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:327:    Reassemble scattered sprites by docking them onto a yellow cross/L anchor whose red tips dictate approach direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:332:    - Red (2) connector pairs appear on sprite boundaries; on the anchor they sit at branch tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:336:    - Remaining sprites translate without rotation. A direct anchor attachment is legal only if a piece covers an entire active anchor tip with the opposite-facing 2-cell port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/42/code.py:340:    - Red pixels are still the assembly pegs, but anchor reds are no longer generic: the side of each anchor tip tells you which side of the first child piece is allowed to dock there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/17/code.py:57:#    - Humans can infer the competition by seeing multiple objects that all contain the legend palette while only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/30/code.py:26:#    The fusion matters because D12 narrows the motif space to a recognizable typed vocabulary, while D3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D6/2/code.py:37:#    grid still contains multiple turning obstacles so the solver must distinguish the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D6/2/code.py:41:#    with multiple x-positions for the same color would be misread as an L-turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/15/code.py:29:#    - The legend border remains a simple bottom-row + right-column L shape in the top-left corner, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/15/code.py:99:    Multiple candidate sizes may exist when the legend is larger, so we keep all legal candidates and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D18/0/code.py:15:#    shape where one moving water pixel can see multiple legal continuations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/14/code.py:40:#       motifs does not create ambiguity between multiple candidate tools.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:297:    assert len(pieces) >= 2, \"input must contain multiple pieces\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:339:    active_tail = _abs_group(_side_red_group(seed[\"arr\"], forward_side), sr0, sc0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:340:    assert len(active_tail) == 2, \"seed must have a 2-cell starting connector\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:345:        moves = _match_group_translations(local_in, active_tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:362:                next_tail = _abs_group(_side_red_group(p[\"arr\"], forward_side), top, left)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:363:                if unpaired != next_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:368:                next_tail = ()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:370:            placed = (nxt, next_rc, next_tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:374:        cur, red_counts, active_tail = placed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D13/1/code.py:95:    - Multiple seeded line networks may now share the same line color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/26/code.py:66:#    cue across multiple rows. That makes the combo visible without adding many unrelated cases.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:60:#   - Deleted regions are built from multiple disconnected objects whose target colors are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:65:#   - _find_legend(...) from the source task assumed an L-shaped frame; that is invalid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:80:#   - There are always multiple color-3 lines, so the solver must distinguish roles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:214:    - A straight color-3 separator line near the top-left acts as the legend divider instead of the original L-shaped frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:216:    - On the main side of the divider, extra color-3 lines further split the board into multiple regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:314:    \"\"\"Split all 3 target colors across multiple objects so only the whole region qualifies.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/0/code.py:62:#    - Multiple sprites may share one anchor color; generator guarantees all such sprites use the same angle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/17/code.py:32:#     - tabs are narrower than the strip, which makes concave/convex shoulders visible without exploding the case count\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D18/1/code.py:46:#      two-cell center basin; they do not need hidden multiplicity tracking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/31/code.py:60:  multiple independent sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/1/code.py:29:#    control multiple sprites, so the same offset can repeat within one grid. We\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/39/code.py:81:    In this combo, the border stays as an L-shaped frame but its size varies with the number of active colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/0/code.py:40:#    - The basin network stays small: a narrow basin beside a wider basin, separated by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/38/code.py:38:#        tips must each accept one more piece. The visible result is two matched\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D12/3/code.py:31:#    multiple sprites, so the rule is neither trivial nor too unconstrained.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D5/1/code.py:43:#   - keeping two nontrivial prototypes plus multiple scales preserves the original matching burden\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/1/code.py:11:#       - a bottom-anchored basin network with a left wall, a low L-shaped divider, and a taller divider;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/2/code.py:74:#      them from two isolated singleton target colors plus multiple copies of a third target color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:18:#   all three together: each sprite now has a 2- or 3-pixel collinear marker set, the effective\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:56:#   and that its 2-3 pixels are collinear; the generator enforces both. It also assumes there is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/16/code.py:29:#   both color identity and multiplicity. This combo uses exactly 4 target colors, with one color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/16/code.py:50:#   That keeps the visual language simple while still making multiplicity observable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/16/code.py:58:# - _find_legend originally returned a set; that would lose multiplicity and break D5. It must now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D9/3/code.py:116:    - bg is the most common color. Two distinct prototype patterns appear as separate sprite components at multiple sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/9/code.py:54:#   - _find_legend in the original solver returned a set; that silently loses multiplicity and is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/9/code.py:215:    tail = cells[1:]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/9/code.py:216:    random.shuffle(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/9/code.py:217:    cells = [cells[0]] + tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/8/code.py:41:#    - Multiple sprites still reuse anchor colors, so the task stays about structured matching rather than one-off color lookup.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/37/code.py:63:    multiple times per grid and becomes learnable from few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/37/code.py:65:    class narrow while still preventing a brittle \"exactly one shape\" shortcut.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:33:#     - 这个变体改为：方向只由容器内部的橙色箭头模板决定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:36:#       具体选左/右或上/下必须看内部箭头\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:38:#     - mover 容器内部至少 3x3，初始橙色永远是一个 4-cell 箭头：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:44:#     - 容器只朝箭头指向的一侧移动；另一侧目标线是显式 decoy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:48:#     - solver 必须先读出内部箭头，例如 right，再只取右侧候选线，随后\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:51:#     - 没把方向做成任意图案，而是固定 4 种箭头模板，复杂度与 ARC 训练样例可观察性匹配\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:58:#       模板推方向，因此 grey-fill 排序也要改成“按箭头所指边 inward”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:69:#     - 箭头模板固定且醒目，2-3 个样例足以归纳“箭头朝哪边就往哪边走”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:74:#     - mover 的 interior orange 恰好等于 1 个箭头模板，因此方向检测唯一\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:93:def _arrow_template(inner_h: int, inner_w: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:118:    base = _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, di