spills from the right source into the narrow central basin; the untouched left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D20/1/code.py:48:#      which keeps the scene readable instead of erasing multiple unrelated layers at once.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D4/0/code.py:47:#   - multiple sprites at mixed scales\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:56:#    - Samples still mix multiple sprites and repeated marker colors, so the solver must infer the axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:14:#     - After solving on the full canvas, the output is cropped to the narrow strip containing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:28:#     - Every anchor gets exactly one sprite. Reusing a center color for multiple sprites would force\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:29:#       multiple bodies to collide on the same target cell, so the generator forbids that.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:128:    - After reconstructing the full solved canvas, keep only the narrow strip that contains the crosshairs and solved sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/21/code.py:170:                raise ValueError(f\"multiple legend components for color {color}\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:104:    out, _details = _solve_variant(grid, return_details=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:108:def _solve_variant(grid: np.ndarray, *, return_details: bool = False) -> tuple[np.ndarray, dict] | np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:226:    details = {\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:235:    if not return_details:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:237:    return out, details\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:863:    solved, details = _solve_variant(inp, return_detai