       tail_len += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D9/1/code.py:716:    return {\"tail_len\": tail_len, \"diag_steps\": diag_steps}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D9/1/code.py:759:            metrics = _tail_metrics(path, fwd)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D9/1/code.py:760:            if metrics[\"tail_len\"] < TAIL_MIN or metrics[\"diag_steps\"] == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/1/code.py:467:    tail = all_candidates[max(6, len(all_candidates) // 2) :]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/1/code.py:468:    random.shuffle(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/1/code.py:469:    ordered = head + tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:742:                is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:743:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:758:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:761:                    tail_r0, tail_r1 = min(prs2), max(prs2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:762:                    tail_c0, tail_c1 = min(pcs2), max(pcs2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:766:                            for r in range(tail_r0, tail_r1 + 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:774:                            for c in range(tail_c0, tail_c1 + 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/31/code.py:69:# - The primary shape always exposes two anchor colors in input and multiple shadow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:3:# Change: 黑色边框矩形容器，内部为灰色/橙色填充，附带同色头部线段指示方向... → 头部为箭头形状而非线段\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:20:# - The moving marker is no longer a 1-cell-thick line. It is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:25:# - The destination marker is an identical arrow sprite of the same color, translated further\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:26:#   along the arrow's pointing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:27:# - To make \"direction from shape\" necessary, the arrow is attached only to a side orthogonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:32:#   Variant logic: an arrow attached above may still point right, so the container moves right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:33:#   The solver must read the arrow shape, then find the matching arrow destination along that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:37:# - The arrow has only four orientations and one fixed size, so the new degree of freedom is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:47:#   the subset of pixels closest to the border. With an arrow sprite, that \"closest layer only\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:48:#   extraction would lose most of the arrow and break matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:50:#   shape, matches it against four fixed arrow templates, and derives direction from that match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:53:# - Each generated object reserves a rectangle covering: input container, input arrow, destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:54:#   arrow, moved container, and moved arrow. Reserved rectangles are packed with a 1-cell margin,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:56:# - The destination arrow is always at least one background cell away from the head arrow, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:60:# - Because the arrow is orthogonally attached, the changed mechanism is visible in every mover:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:65:# - Only three object types remain on the board: container, source arrow, destination arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:66:#   The arrow is compact (3x3), monochrome, and separated from other assemblies by background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:70:#   cue that the viewer has to infer is the arrow orientation itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:114:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int, attach_side: str, anchor: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:124:def _stamp_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, tl: tuple[int, int], direction: str, color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:141:    Move bordered containers toward same-colored arrow destinations, charging grey cells to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:144:    - The source marker is a 3x3 arrow sprite, not a line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:145:    - Direction is derived from the arrow's normalized shape, not from which side of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:146:      container the arrow touches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:147:    - The container and arrow translate toward the nearest matching arrow destination along\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:148:      the arrow direction, capped by the number of grey interior cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:342:        head_r, head_c = _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h, outer_w, attach_side, anchor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:442:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (hr, hc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:443:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (dr, dc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:474:        _stamp_arrow(expected, (nhr, nhc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_comb