xed center ink pixel and a second tip pixel:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D18/2/code.py:323:    - down-right tip: diagonal exit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D18/2/code.py:324:    - down tip: straight-forward exit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D18/2/code.py:325:    - right tip: orthogonal exit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:23:    - Original: two L-shaped outside pieces could never exist, because two L-shaped holes were forbidden.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:24:    - Variant: two L-shaped holes may both exist. One hole touches a red wall marker, the other touches blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:36:  - Candidate matching by `area + exact downsampled mask` is still valid, but now may yield multiple pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:46:    from accidentally signaling multiple holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D1/2/code.py:18:#    The scene still shows one 3-pixel L marker and several scattered filled rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/23/code.py:31:#    - D13/0: growth stops only when the tail touches the outer grid boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/23/code.py:36:#      tail (width 6): no longer depends on cavity filling, attaches flush farther outward and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/23/code.py:41:#      tail rows: depth 4 has ######, depths 5..8 keep only the new outer anchor cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/23/code.py:59:#    - \"tail should have no remaining cavity\" is no longer a useful termination predicate; the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/23/code.py:74:#    tail to be legible. The bar remains the single dominant object; decoys stay on the bar and do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/23/code.py:93:#      empty cavity\" logic would miss the true tail.\n/