xinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/1/code.py:18:#      so its L shape exactly overlays that station's visible orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/1/code.py:49:#   3. The grid avoids stacking multiple cue systems on the same cells: labels do matching, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/2/code.py:59:    - B pieces are narrow rectangles placed far enough from the notch columns to avoid overlap inside bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:10:      - two 3-pixel L-corners on one bbox diagonal, or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:25:      - expected L-shaped anchors at bbox corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:90:      This is structurally signposted in the input, so even when multiple colors appear, the mapping is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/2/code.py:15:#      2) Multiple movers are no longer independent. We first compute every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/5/code.py:9:#   Fused: the anchor carries a 2- or 3-pixel grey line at its corner. After rotating\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:35:#    2-3 sprites are sampled so multiple examples support \"inner color chooses\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d59b0160/D17/1/code.py:45:#    - Samples always contain multiple matching components, and at least one smaller matching component survives.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/0/code.py:23:#     - old flow: detect plus component -> find adjacent seed -> use arm-tip span as nozzle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/0/code.py:37:#     - the old arm-tip alignment asserts are invalid because frames have no arm nozzles;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/0/code.py:41:#     - different objects must neither overlap nor 4-touch each other, otherwise multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D8/2/code.py:105:        # Prefer the strongest base-task signatures if multiple colors somehow pass:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/11/code.py:67:   - Exactly one station group has multiple 4-connected lobes, and every train docks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:17:#    head turns into an 8-colored tip and the former bulk turns into 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:677:    tip_r, tip_c = HEAD_TIPS[direction]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:682:        target_tip = (r0 - gap, random.randint(c0, c1) + jitter)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:684:        target_tip = (r1 + gap, random.randint(c0, c1) + jitter)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:686:        target_tip = (random.randint(r0, r1) + jitter, c0 - gap)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:688:        target_tip = (random.randint(r0, r1) + jitter, c1 + gap)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:689:    dr = target_tip[0] - tip_r\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:690:    dc = target_tip[1] - tip_c\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:3:# Change: '+'精灵为小型中心对称色块（3x3十字、3x4胖十字、5x4胖菱形等），bbox至少3x3，左右+上下对称... → 箭头形精灵\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:10:# - The shared anchor color now forms several small arrow blobs instead of plus-like symmetric blobs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:11:# - Each arrow is one of a few fixed templates, rotated to point U/D/L/R.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:12:# - Each arrow still owns exactly one colored seed tile and one grid keeps one ray pre-extended.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:14:#   (clockwise from the pointing direction), while the arrow's own facing direction tells us where the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:15:#   ray should go. Example: a right-pointing arrow has its seed directly below it, but the seed repeats\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:17:#   we must read the arrow shape and project \"right\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:19:# - If the seed stayed on the tip side, the task would visually collapse back toward the original.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:24:# - Each generated grid uses at least two arrow orientations so the orientation cue is actually visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:26:# - detect_dominant_big_component_color still works because arrows remain the only components with both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:30:# - The original nozzle-span assert also depended on a plus arm/tip model and is no longer meaningful.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:35:#   wrong arrow and the solver sees exactly one adjacent non-arrow component per arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:37:#   existing arrow-neighborhood guard cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:39:# - Human-solvable cue: arrows visibly point one way while their seed sits on a different side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:40:# - The kept pre-extended ray demonstrates that the repeated pattern follows the arrow orientation, not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:44:# - Rays do not overlap arrows and do not touch foreign arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:51:# - For every generated arrow, the unique attachment side must be orthogonal to the ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:52:# - Per sample, at least two distinct arrow orientations should usually appear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:54:# - Solver assumes every big anchor component exactly matches one rotated arrow template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:55:# - Solver assumes each arrow has exactly one adjacent non-anchor component (seed or pre-extended ray).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:177:        \"launch\": (2, 2),  # canonical right-arrow: seed attaches below this cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:207:_CANONICAL_ATTACH_NORMAL = (1, 0)  # right-arrow seeds attach on the clockwise flank: below\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:255:def _oriented_arrow_spec(spec: dict, direction: str) -> tuple[np.ndarray, tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:262:def _match_arrow_direction(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:299:    Extend marker tiles forward from arrow-shaped anchors by repeating them to the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:303:    - A dominant non-bg color forms several small arrow sprites, possibly in different rotations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:304:    - Each arrow has exactly one adjacent colored marker component; one of these rays may already be long.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:307:    - For each arrow, recognize which way the arrow points from its shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:309:    - Repeat that payload in the arrow's pointing direction until the boundary, without overwriting arrow pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:311:    Key insight: The marker's attachment side is no longer the direction cue; the arrow silhouette itself\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:319:    arrow_col = detect_dominant_big_component_color(g, bg=bg, min_h=3, min_w=3, connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:320:    if arrow_col is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:323:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_col), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:324:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_col))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:328:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:329:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:330:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:333:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:334:        local_arrow = g[int(ar0):int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0):int(ac1) + 1] == int(arrow_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:335:        direction = _match_arrow_direction(local_arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:340:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:366:            protect={int(arrow_col)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:372:# --------------- generator (D4 arrow variant) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:514:def _mark_arrow_guard(guard: np.ndarray, cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:525:def _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:533:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:535:    arrow_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:537:    patch, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:546:        arrow_cells = _component_cells(patch, (r0, c0))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:548:        if not _cells_have_gap(arrow_cells, occ):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:563:            if int(occ[rr, cc]) != 0 or bool(arrow_guard[rr, cc]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:569:        for rr, cc in arrow_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:571:            out[rr, cc] = int(arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:572:        _mark_arrow_guard(arrow_guard, arrow_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:593:    arrows: list[dict],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:597:    pre_idx = max(range(len(arrows)), key=lambda i: arrows[i][\"tiles\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:598:    if arrows[pre_idx][\"tiles\"] < _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:599:        candidates = [i for i, meta in enumerate(arrows) if meta[\"tiles\"] >= _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:604:    for i, meta in enumerate(arrows):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:630:    arrow_color = int(rng.choice(others))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:631:    palette = [c for c in others if c != arrow_color]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:639:    arrow_guard = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:641:    arrows: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:643:        meta = _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:651:            arrow_guard,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:653:            arrow_color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:657:        arrows.append(meta)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:659:    inp = _build_input_from_output(out, arrows, bg, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/19/code.py:50:#      color becomes the target fill. This is visible across multiple samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D7/2/code.py:27:#     - 形状族控制在 3 类：角落对角线、角落直角三角形、角落四边形；自由度不大，但足够\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:3:# Name: 内部图案决定方向加箭头头部\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:21:# - Outside the container there is now a 3x3 maroon arrow head plus a matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:22:#   3x3 maroon destination arrow further along the travel direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:25:#     2. Use the external arrow only as the movable head sprite and as a visual\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:27:# - To make that visible, the head arrow is always attached on a side orthogonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:30:#     * internal orange cells form a right-pointing arrow template\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:31:#     * external arrow head also points right, but it is attached above or below\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:34:#       destination arrow to the right of the source arrow, then move container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:38:#     * fused: internal orange arrow decides direction, head position is decoupled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:39:#       from direction, and the head itself is a compact arrow sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:43:# - The internal cue is a fixed 4-cell arrow template, not an arbitrary shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:44:# - The external cue is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:53:#   still keep its identity. Broken: a 3x3 arrow must be tracked as a full shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:55:#   must depend on the internal arrow direction instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:56:# - New assumption introduced here: movers have a unique internal arrow template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:60:# - New assumption introduced here: the external arrow direction agrees with the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:61:#   internal arrow direction. Generator guarantees this and solver checks it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:65:#     input container, input head arrow, destination arrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:66:#     moved container, moved head arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:70:#   arrows from appearing between a source head and its own destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:76:# - The head arrow points the same way as the internal motif, acting as a second\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:81:# - Each assembly contains one container, one source arrow, one destination arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:83:#   head lands exactly on its destination arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:87:# - Orange growth is structurally tied to the same inferred direction: the arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:92:#   old same-side head as an arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:131:def _arrow_template(inner_h: int, inner_w: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:156:    base = _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:185:        template = set(_arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:193:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int,