orted by the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D11/0/code.py:55:# - The nozzle-span alignment checks assume the seed tile is flush with the arm tip. Generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D11/0/code.py:200:    own multiple independent seeds, and each seed defines its own ray by attachment side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D13/0/code.py:30:#      multiple times. The generator guarantees a symmetric tile with all four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D3/2/code.py:199:    - Away from the legend, a marker color appears either as two opposite L-shaped corners of one bounding box or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:35:# - At least one legend entry is reused across multiple bands, ensuring the partitioned processing is visible and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:60:# - The three fused signals are all directly visible: multiple background bands, an off-corner edge legend, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:71:#   same actual marker color in multiple bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:14:     * D2: a 3-pixel outer segment emits from all 3 segment pixels, not only its two ends;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:31:   - To keep the combo legible, the generator only allows full 3-pixel segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:57:   - For each chosen edge, the generator builds the 3-pixel segment, then computes three full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:180:    - Each outer segment is a straight 3-pixel diagonal component in its own color, separate from the diamond color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/14/code.py:38:#    - Original / D14 code assumed either multiple markers or a unique orthogonal mate could be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D3/4/code.py:74:#   - proximity grouping is supported by repeated examples because multiple top objects use the same rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D7/0/code.py:29:#    - The alignment asserts still depend on each seed bbox matching the arm-tip span exactly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D7/0/code.py:227:            # Alignment check: seed cross-axis span must match arm tip span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:79:     same legend row applies to multiple repeated strips of one marker color, the direction code gets\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:381:    - The L shapes no longer tell you the diagonal to fill. They only provide coordinates for axis-aligned pairing; the diagonal choice is encoded visibly in the legend's left-versus-right color order and reused across several same-colored pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:431:# ── CFG: per-entry multiplicity ────────────────────────────────────\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D17/0/code.py:47:#    - Generated examples are rejected unless top-down and bottom-up execution differ by multiple cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D1/1/code.py:32:#     - Because each sample contains two types with repeated markers or repeated source copies, the \"majority color is the key\" rule is supported multiple times within one grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/3/code.py:202:    The visible point is already the chosen emitting endpoint, not the midpoint of a hidden 3-pixel segment,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D12/2/code.py:72:#     - When there are multiple wrong cells, generation forces a mix of background and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D6/2/code.py:48:#    - The repeated mirrored blocks along the scaled perimeter create multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D17/0/code.py:64:#   subcomponents reserve their own narrower interval in their matched bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:9:      - Each legend color usually marked one rectangle via two opposite 3-pixel L-corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:28:      - The top cross has an upward extra tip; the bottom cross has a downward extra tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:43:      - Cross markers are larger and come in multiple scales.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:63:      - `_l_anchor_present(...)` assumed sparse 3-pixel L-corners at bbox corners. Directed crosses violate that.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:81:      - A base arm length k needs margin k+1 from every border to allow the extra tip in any direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:601:    and multiple arm lengths when the grid has enough cross entries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/24/code.py:23:#   and no multiple canvas sizes. To keep the change visually obvious, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/7/code.py:54:#    - The generator demands multiple skipped cells and multiple diamond-colored ray pixels,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D1/4/code.py:74:      destination holds only tiny 2-3 pixel connector components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D9/2/code.py:36:#    biases toward 3-5 cavity rows and requires at least two rows with multiple cavities via\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D9/2/code.py:58:#    generator uses distinct colors per row, not per cavity, and prefers plans with multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D9/2/code.py:317:# Plans are curated so multiple rows usually contain repeated same-row evidence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:22:#   one legend row acts multiple times, overlap priority is reversed, and marker/legend preservation disappears.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:31:#   multiple pairs plus distractors. The original hard-coded L-anchor logic is also invalid because marker shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:41:#   Humans can see all driving cues directly: one legend row maps a color to a fill; the same row has multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:50:#   The solver assumes every useful marker color splits into components whose normalized-shape multiplicities are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:51:#   only 1 or 2, with at least two multiplicity-2 groups. The generator guarantees that by construction. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:52:#   solver also assumes each multiplicity-2 group occupies exactly one bbox diagonal; the generator places every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:203:    multiplicities = {shape: len(group) for shape, group in shape_groups.items()}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:204:    assert all(count in (1, 2) for count in multiplicities.values()), \"shape multiplicities must be 1 or 2\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:219:    return marker_mask, pair_infos, multiplicities\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:305:# ── CFG: per-entry multiplicity ────────────────────────────────────\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:519:        _, pair_infos, multiplicities = _entry_pair_infos(g, int(marker), legend_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/19/code.py:523:        if any(count == 1 for count in multiplicities.values()):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/17/code.py:15:# - A direct reuse of the original \"3 pixels, clipped to 2 by the boundary\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/17/code.py:153:    - Each outer segment is 2 or 3 pixels long and uses its own non-background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/18/code.py:95:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/3/code.py:24:#   The generator forces both action colors to appear multiple times and forces the tile to be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D3/0/code.py:43:#      sprite multiple times per block and shift placements incorrectly. The loop must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/4/code.py:32:    one distinct fill claim -> that fill color; multiple distinct fill claims ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/4/code.py:111:- If multiple entries claim the same background cell with the same fill color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/4/code.py:432:    - Away from the legend, each marker color appears as one diagonal pair of L-shaped corner marks;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/0/code.py:600:                is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/0/code.py:601:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/0/code.py:616:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D4/0/code.py:42:# - Original generator protected a wedge-shaped area tailored to that scan path. Once the legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/25/code.py:109:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D3/1/code.py:60:#     - only 2-3 border markers are used, so even when a stamp colors multiple edge cells, the frame stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/5/code.py:46:    - The original 2x2 recolor branch is invalid because every active entry now has exactly 3 pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/5/code.py:60:    - Thin bands create much less clutter than full-triangle fills, which helps when multiple entries coexist.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D4/1/code.py:62:  Widths stay in a narrow range and fills remain unique, preventing ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D4/1/code.py:144:    - Elsewhere, each marker color appears either as two opposite L-shaped bbox corners or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/26/code.py:42:#     can see the same source color propagated into multiple destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/26/code.py:225:        assert sid not in used, \"destination sprites should not receive multiple leaves\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/3/code.py:69:#     - Each cavity uses only two colors, repeated across multiple cells by the checkerboard,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:12:#    - Small trace: suppose a TR outer segment is the 3-pixel diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:26:#      boundary. A 2-pixel segment is a contiguous subsegment of the canonical 3-pixel outer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:29:#      (4-step vs 6-step bundles) and at least one 3-pixel segment where D2 is visibly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:55:#    - A human sees two repeated regularities: 3-pixel segments produce denser 3-lane bundles\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:14:#    - Example: if the left chain uses colors [2, 4, 6] from root to tail and the right chain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:723:                is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:724:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:739:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D4/2/code.py:70:#       borders, and occupy multiple row bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/13/code.py:41:#       ambiguous because a full rectangle can accidentally satisfy multiple L-corner tests. The generator therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D11/0/code.py:75:# - Multiple colors are preserved exactly; there is no hidden recoloring map to guess.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D11/0/code.py:107:    - Its bbox patch `sprite` may contain multiple colors and background holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/31/code.py:218:    assert len(sprites) >= 3, \"expected multiple bordered sprites\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/15/code.py:55:# - The rule space is intentionally narrow: exactly one component, one mask, and exactly 2 rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/15/code.py:122:    - Its cropped patch `sprite` may contain multiple colors and background holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/16/code.py:15:#       same_geometry: 3-pixel diagonal segment (or 2 if clipped) one step outside a diamond edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D12/1/code.py:15:#   - The rule is unchanged, but the same color can now play multiple roles at once, so the grid is visually more ambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D6/1/code.py:53:#   multiple of 3; the generator preserves that exactly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/23/code.py:49:#    - Distractors are removed, but multiple legend entries remain and their bboxes are packed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D9/0/code.py:42:#     - the variant is only visible if split pixels are numerous enough and touch multiple regions, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:18:#   depth 1 is recolored to the \"next\" legend color, and a depth-2 tail is recolored to the second-next\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:770:                is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:771:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:786:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D13/1/code.py:41:      to be genuine L-pairs whose fill masks overlap on multiple background cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D13/1/code.py:306:    - Outside the legend, each marker color appears either as two L-shaped opposite corners of a bbox or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/27/code.py:163:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:26:#    - Fill colors are intentionally reused across multiple cavities, so solving cannot collapse\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:16:#     old: 2-3 pixel diagonal segment, one per chosen diamond edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:17:#     new: 3-pixel L marker occupying three cells of a 2x2 block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:22:#     new: infer outward diagonal directly from the L bend orientation; the two degree-1 tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:23:#          emit rays, and the ray direction is the sum of the two unit arm vectors from bend to tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:31:#     从 bend 到两个 tips 的单位向量分别是 (-1,0) 和 (0,+1)，其和为 (-1,+1)，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:40:#     - 原 _outer_line_info 假设外部组件共线；L 标记下完全失效，必须用 4 邻域度数找 bend/tips。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:58:#     这样输入里每个局部结构都很清楚：一个 5x5 方框，周围若干小 L，输出再从对应 tips 拉出对角线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:63:#     - marker 必须是 3 像素、4 邻域下唯一 bend + 两个 tips 的 L；生成器只放这种模板。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:65:#     - 射线方向必须是 tips 相对 bend 的两个单位向量之和；模板构造保证恰好得到四个非轴向对角方向。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:136:    tips = [p for p, d in deg.items() if d == 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:137:    if len(bends) != 1 or len(tips) != 2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:141:    arm_vecs = [(tr - bend[0], tc - bend[1]) for tr, tc in tips]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:153:        \"tips\": sorted(tips),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:169:    Extend diagonal rays from L-shaped corner markers around hollow square rings on a checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:177:    - For each L marker, find the unique bend cell of 4-neighbor degree 2 and the two degree-1 tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:178:    - The diagonal ray direction is the sum of the two unit vectors from the bend to those tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:179:      Starting from each tip, paint background cells in that direction with the marker color until\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:223:            for pr, pc in minfo[\"tips\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:301:        tips = list(info[\"tips\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:303:        rays = _ray_cells((h, w), tips[0], outward) + _ray_cells((h, w), tips[1], outward)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:14:      - replace the single global grey trail with multiple disconnected grey components\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:115:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:240:    - Grey cells form multiple disconnected thin path components, and each component touches an ordered chain of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:263:    assert len(grey_comps) >= 2, \"expected multiple grey components\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:44:#    objects inside a narrow interior activity strip aligned with the long grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:46:#    input, and preserves multiple repeated examples of the same rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:68:#    Active objects share one narrow strip but do not overlap after expansion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Pick a long-thin bbox sized to fit multiple visible objects in one strip.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D18/1/code.py:293:    - Most legend markers appear as two opposite L-shaped corners plus one separate same-color direction pixel on the bbox edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/1/code.py:248:            raise ValueError(\"shape multiplicity mismatch\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:16:#    - Original task: a hollow diamond has a short 3-pixel diagonal segment outside each chosen edge;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:19:#      become the arm tips N/S/W/E, and the natural rays become cardinal instead of diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:20:#    - D6 then compresses each 3-pixel outer segment into its center pixel only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:21:#    - Fused result: each chosen arm keeps only one point marker one step beyond the arm tip:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:23:#      The point is interpreted as the midpoint of the hidden 3-pixel segment that would have appeared\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:26:#    - Difference from source: shape reasoning switches from diamond edges to plus arm tips, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:140:    - Zero or more single-pixel markers, each sitting just beyond one arm tip of a plus.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:143:    - Treat each marker as the midpoint of a hidden 3-pixel segment orthogonal to that arm's ray direction.\n/home/lixi