tiple objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D8/0/code.py:30:#     cells are on the outward tip row/column, so the next piece has a unique cavity to fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D8/0/code.py:49:#   - The original generator's tail-zero-cavity condition is not solver-enforced. Under one-sided\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:13:# a) Concrete behavior: in the base task a 3-pixel outer segment emits two rays that keep going\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:17:# b) Complexity calibration: the multiplier is global and fixed at 2, while each grid uses only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:25:#      clipping and keeps one extra empty step beyond every ray tip to separate this combo from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:164:    tail_r = start[0] + dr * (ray_len + 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:165:    tail_c = start[1] + dc * (ray_len + 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:166:    if not (0 <= tail_r < h and 0 <= tail_c < w):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:173:    Decode each outer diagonal segment's length and emit two rays whose lengths are a fixed multiple of it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/2/code.py:21:#      explicitly tells the sprite's role in its chain: 1=root, 2=middle, 3=tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/2/code.py:40:#      That fails here because marker dots split each sprite into multiple monochrome\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/2/code.py:78:    chain order: 1-dot root, 2-dot middle, 3-dot tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/2/code.py:743:                is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/2/code.py:744:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/2/code.py:775:                if is_tail and remaining:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/2/code.py:777:                if not is_tail and not remaining:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:19:#    therefore not a new visual primitive; it is that one legend color now controls multiple distant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:25:#    To make the D14 change visible in 2-4 examples, every active legend entry has multiple L-pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:31:#    immediately when the same color labels multiple rectangles. It also relies on a single diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:43:#    which colors have 2 versus 3 pairs, so the \"same marker color applies multiple times\" pattern is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:51:#    based sorting is introduced. The only new inference is multiplicity: one legend mapping applies\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:308:    - The legend mapping is reused multiple times per color: the hard part is not the fill itself, but discovering which same-colored L-corners belong together before applying one shared fill color to every matched rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:356:# ── CFG: per-entry multiplicity ────────────────────────────────────\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/11/code.py:123:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D10/1/code.py:31:#      pixels act as round-2 markers; round 2 creates more relay pixels, and so on until the chain tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/8/code.py:44:   - Baseline color appears in multiple separated runs on the baseline row because bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/8/code.py:53:     width. After narrowing the baseline, a tall bar can rival that count. Fix: detect\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/8/code.py:54:     the row/color that forms multiple separated runs, which matches the overwritten\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D5/1/code.py:96:    Input is multiple frames concatenated horizontally, separated by full-height\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D5/1/code.py:229:        f\"head={head} dir={d}: markers reachable in multiple directions \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D5/1/code.py:404:    multiples = [n for n in range(*STEPS_RANGE) if n % n_frames == 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D5/1/code.py:405:    weights = np.array([(n ** 3) / (_STEP_AVAILABILITY[n] ** 2) for n in multiples], dtype=float)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D5/1/code.py:407:    n_steps = int(rng.choice(multiples, p=weights))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/5/code.py:40:#    - cells hit by multiple rays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D8/1/code.py:51:    - that cavity spans a strip exactly 1 cell narrower than the previous piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D8/1/code.py:630:            is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D8/1/code.py:631:            next_span = spans[piece_idx + 1] if not is_tail else None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D8/1/code.py:673:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/0/code.py:14:#     old: 3-pixel diagonal segment outside one diamond edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/0/code.py:15:#     new: 3-pixel horizontal/vertical segment centered outside one square side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/0/code.py:38:#   - Outer segments stay short (3 pixels) so adjacent sides do not merge under 8-connectivity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/0/code.py:50:#     incorrectly merge at corners if they touched there, so the generator centers each 3-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/37/code.py:661:        tail = list(int_pos)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/37/code.py:662:        random.shuffle(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/37/code.py:663:        pool.extend(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/6/code.py:60:- Control masks are connected, contain real holes, span multiple rows and cols, and include both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D7/0/code.py:22:#      color now appears multiple times, so one source sprite type must be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D7/0/code.py:67:#      multiple identical stamps in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D7/0/code.py:103:      may mark multiple destination cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D13/1/code.py:57:    non-local comparison across multiple candidate regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/0/code.py:30:#     - at least one non-tail piece has zero cavity and is not on the boundary, so the sample\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/0/code.py:40:#       root-notch matching rather than from multiple independent rule families.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/0/code.py:467:    tail = pieces[-1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/0/code.py:468:    if side == \"top\" and not any(r == 0 for r, _ in tail):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/0/code.py:470:    if side == \"bottom\" and not any(r == H - 1 for r, _ in tail):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/0/code.py:472:    if side == \"left\" and not any(c == 0 for _, c in tail):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/0/code.py:474:    if side == \"right\" and not any(c == W - 1 for _, c in tail):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:29:#     - they are the plus's four arm tips: N / S / W / E\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:31:#     - N/S arms use a horizontal 3-pixel segment one cell beyond the arm tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:32:#     - W/E arms use a vertical 3-pixel segment one cell beyond the arm tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:37:#     - therefore the four arm tips correspond to the four cardinal ray directions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:41:#     - a diagonal 3-pixel segment sits parallel to one diamond edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:45:#     - a top-arm segment is horizontal and sits directly above the top arm tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:49:#     - edge-based diagonal reasoning is replaced by tip-based axial reasoning\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D5/1/code.py:134:    - Short horizontal/vertical segments in another non-bg color, each adjacent to one arm tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/7/code.py:129:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/11/code.py:77:#      - the upper and lower tails move together as one asymmetric shape, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/28/code.py:25:#    - Original generator assumed the same 3-pixel outer segment everywhere; here segment geometry must be rebuilt\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:27:#    - The chain stops only when the tail piece leaves zero cavity in its own bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:36:#    - Therefore output examples visibly differ from the original task: the grey tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:42:#      tail(green) fills blue's cavity and leaves no cavity, so stop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:44:#      tail(grey) fills blue's cavity, extends, but still leaves 1-6 bg cells in its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:51:#      every grey tail. If grey tails also had zero cavity, the new control variable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:63:#    - Old generator tail branch forced zero residual cavity. That directly encodes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:64:#      old D13 value and is replaced by a grey tail with positive residual cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:69:#    - Every chain piece spans the same strip width as before. The grey tail still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:75:#    - More importantly, grey tails still contain black holes in the output; this makes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D13/2/code.py:79:#    - No extra overlay markers are added. The marker is the whole tail piece color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:33:#    - A crucial hidden detail: one L-pair is itself disconnected. A raw 4-connected split yields two corner pieces,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:43:#    - The crucial visible change is repetition: one legend row controls multiple same-color marker objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:53:#    - Because the same marker color is reused across multiple objects, a solver can infer that the legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:223:    - The legend no longer selects among multiple colors; instead, one color rule is reused repeatedly,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/13/code.py:131:    - Multiple hollow 8-pixel diamonds in distinct non-background colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D9/0/code.py:39:#    - One extra tail marker is always left after the hidden output snapshot so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D9/0/code.py:81:    Input is multiple frames concatenated horizontally, separated by full-height\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D9/0/code.py:199:        f\"head={head} dir={d}: markers reachable in multiple directions \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D9/0/code.py:640:            \