combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:19:#   source.arrow -> dominant-axis direction to the target destination,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:32:#   in the encoded arrow direction. So arrow direction alone is insufficient.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:34:#   corners compatible with the chosen arrow direction. This keeps the symbolic alphabet small.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:42:#   that border class and then resolve the target by arrow direction plus marker quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:43:# - The D15-style directional cue is compressed to a 2-pixel center+neighbor arrow stub. That\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:46:#   3-pixel arrow while remaining a single readable object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:51:# - Sources are always fully visible 3x3 boxes so both the arrow and the diagonal marker are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:53:# - Source placement is filtered so the two destinations are both in the source's arrow direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:58:# - The input visibly contains two deleted source boxes, each with an arrow and an extra corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:65:# - The arrow is a compact 2-pixel center+edge pointer, while the marker remains a single corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:74:# - Real sources are full 3x3 boxes with color multiplicities exactly {6,2,1}: guaranteed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:75:# - For each real source, both destinations share the arrow direction but occupy the two marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:152:    assert patch[mr, mc] == border_color, \"marker corner must not overlap the arrow\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/c