ers, triggers, and emitted rays must stay in-bounds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:61:#    - Marker cells are chosen only from the two free orthogonal neighbors in front of each tip;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:62:#      they may touch exactly one blue cell: their own tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:68:#      1. blue L-shapes identify arrow tips and directions;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:69:#      2. repeated marker colors identify which distant arrows pair up;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:78:#      marker-tip relation readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:127:    assert dr != 0 and abs(dr) == abs(dc), \"tips must form a 45-degree diagonal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:144:def _arrow_cells(tip: tuple[int, int], direction: tuple[int, int]) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:145:    r, c = tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:150:def _forward_marker_candidates(tip: tuple[int, int], direction: tuple[int, int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:151:    r, c = tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:156:def _parse_arrow_component(comp: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:164:    tip = next(cell for cell, d in deg.items() if d == 2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:165:    rels = [(rr - tip[0], cc - tip[1]) for rr, cc in comp if (rr, cc) != tip]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:175:    return tip, (dr, dc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:178:def _find_arrow_sources(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/s