mponents with non-uniform sizes, so \"count components\" and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/28/code.py:137:    - Let the repeat count equal the total number of color-3 pixels in section 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/27/code.py:239:      contribute multiple dots, so fewer big sprites can outscore more small ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/27/code.py:19:#    - D17/0 is narrowed by the fusion description: only the unmarked spectator lanes turn grey, rather than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:27:#    is enough repetition for humans to notice \"one sprite <- multiple isolated pixels\" without\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:152:    tip_12 = [flag for _, flag in out_info]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:186:    for ep, d, is_12 in zip(endpoints, out_dirs, tip_12):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:389:    Flood the wall enclosure, then let multiple singleton movers carve outward tunnels and recolor any obstacle sprite they hit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:442:def _make_arm(depth, start_v, target_v, extra_steps, tip_12=False):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:447:        if tip_12:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:506:    tip_12 = depth >= 2 * max_n_side and random.random() < TIP_12_PROB\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:507:    left = _make_arm(depth, 0, left_bottom, extra_l, tip_12=tip_12)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/16/code.py:508:    right = _make_arm(depth, gap, right_bottom, extra_r, tip_12=tip_12)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:53:#    multiple regions provides enough evidence for the global rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:226:# - The rule is only interesting when multiple regions contribute, so generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/11/code.py:20:# Using a clean multiplier keeps the D6 change visible while still leaving\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/11/code.py:45:#    fixed multiplier keeps the encoded parameter simple and countable while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:7:#    - 保留原题对象：3 像素 L 形箭头、单色墙、对角线射线、撞墙换色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:8:#    - 新增 D6 编码：每个箭头后方的反向对角线上放同色 tail；tail 长度 = 该箭头真实前进总步数。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:11:#    - 小例子：若 tail=9，真实三段长度为 4,3,2，则 solver 实际走 9 步；输出只显影\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:17:#    - 每张图至少放 1 支“三段主箭”，让 3,2,1 同时出现；其他箭再混入 1-3 段与不同 tail 长度，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:18:#      让“数 tail 决定总步数”也有重复支撑。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:20:#    - 原 solver 假设所有非箭头非背景像素都是墙；融合后 tail 不是墙，必须先从同色箭头后方剥离。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:21:#    - 原 solver 假设终止由出界保证；融合后终止由 tail 计数保证，所以状态里必须跟踪 `steps_used`。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:27:#    - tail、箭头、墙、真实路径、以及“本可继续前进的一格”都预留占位，防止固定步数与出界终止退化成同一件事。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:30:#    - 终点前方至少再留 1 个可走对角格，所以输出会在网格内部停止，tail 的计数作用清晰可见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:32:#    - tail 放在箭头背后且不与箭头 4 连通；墙颜色与箭头颜色分离；不同箭对象之间用 `blocked` 留出缓冲。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:33:#    - 输出只出现箭头、tail、墙、少量显影前缀和反射点，不会被整条隐藏路径搅乱。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:36:#    - tail 只编码数量，不编码颜色语义；同色 tail 与同色箭头一一配对，数数即可。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:41:#    - 假设：tail 是箭头同色、连续、位于反向对角线。generator 始终这样构造，并强制箭头颜色唯一。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:42:#    - 假设：墙不会复用箭头颜色。generator 从剩余颜色中取墙色，避免 tail 计数误吸收墙。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:66:def _is_arrow_pts(pts: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:74:def _arrow_dir_start_missing(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:99:def _arrow_points(start_r: int, start_c: int, dr: int, dc: int) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int]], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:110:def _tail_points(start_r: int, start_c: int, dr: int, dc: int, steps: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:119:def _min_segment_lengths(n_bounces: int, rich_arrow: bool) -> list[int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:123:    if rich_arrow and parts == 3:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:128:def _sample_segment_lengths(total_steps: int, n_bounces: int, rich_arrow: bool) -> list[int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:130:    mins = _min_segment_lengths(int(n_bounces), bool(rich_arrow))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:161:    Trace diagonal rays from L-arrows, stop after a tail-encoded step budget,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:168:    arrows: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:169:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:173:            if not _is_arrow_pts(pts):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:175:            info = _arrow_dir_start_missing(pts)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:179:            arrows.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:188:            arrow_cells |= set(pts)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:191:    for arrow in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:192:        color = int(arrow[\"colo