/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D10/2/code.py:68:#     - multiple clusters in one grid visibly show \"same source color, different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:19:#    blockers. Here each wall-sprite still fills/radiates first, but multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:35:#    to show \"multiple movers per source\" and \"different targets recolored\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:130:    tip_12 = [flag for _, flag in out_info]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:139:        \"tip_12\": tip_12,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:189:    for ep, d, is_12 in zip(sprite[\"endpoints\"], sprite[\"out_dirs\"], sprite[\"tip_12\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:383:    Fill several half-enclosed sprites, then let multiple isolated pixels travel into other sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:394:    - If multiple pixels hit the same target, the later arrival wins; in these grids that is the pixel with the longer travel distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:397:    - The task is no longer \"one wall + passive blockers\". You must detect multiple sprites, match each mover to the sprite behind it, and treat the first sprite ahead as an absorption target whose fill region inherits the final incoming color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:426:def _make_arm(depth: int, start_v: int, target_v: int, extra_steps: int, tip_12: bool = False) -> list[Coord]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:431:        if tip_12:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:481:    tip_12 = depth >= 2 * max_n_side and random.random() < TIP_12_PROB\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/36/code.py:482:    left = _make_arm(depth, 0, left_bottom, extra_l, tip_12=tip_12)\n/home/lixinyu/s