, start_v, target_v, extra_steps, tip_12=False):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:465:        if tip_12:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:525:    tip_12 = depth >= 2 * max_n_side and random.random() < TIP_12_PROB\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:526:    left = _make_arm(depth, 0, left_bottom, extra_l, tip_12=tip_12)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:527:    right = _make_arm(depth, gap, right_bottom, extra_r, tip_12=tip_12)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/12/code.py:24:  create repeated recursive crossings and multiple enclosed diamonds, but keeps the palette\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/10/code.py:28:     both multiplicity of trunks and explicit two-sided enclosure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/10/code.py:46:     multiple starts were added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/10/code.py:62:   - Multiple green seeds are already visible in the input, so the learner can anticipate multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/10/code.py:87:     are actually active: there must be multiple starts, and every start must participate in every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/10/code.py:168:    assert starts.shape[0] >= 2, \"canonical input must retain multiple starts\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/10/code.py:246:    - Multiple green (3) pixels lie on one border edge and mark several simultaneous path starts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D6/2/code.py:70:#       the same distance-color pattern multiple times.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:18:#   in a 2x2 box, and walls are still mono-color 1-pixel or 3-pixel side segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:19:# - To fuse D6 and D17 without breaking arrow detection, each arrow now carries two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:21:#     1) reverse-diagonal tail behind the missing corner, length = EXTRA_STEPS.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:22:#     2) mirrored diagonal tail behind the other side of the arrow, length = SEG_LEN.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:24:#   connected to the arrow itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:36:#       A = arrow color, B = current inherited color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:40:#     arrow color 2, SEG_LEN=5, EXTRA_STEPS=4, first turn hits wall color 7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:49:#   wall-turn arrow and one auto-turn arrow, rather than forcing every arrow to do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:50:#   both. That keeps the scene readable and avoids impossible long-tail geometries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:51:# - The wall-turn arrow uses SEG_LEN=5 and EXTRA_STEPS=4 so the post-wall segment\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:52:#   is long enough to expose the AABB pattern. The auto-turn arrow uses smaller\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:58:# - Original `wall_cells = all non-bg non-arrow` no longer works, because marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:59:#   tails would be mistaken for walls. The solver must parse markers first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:71:# - Generator is output-first. It reserves arrow cells plus both marker tails before\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:73:# - Rays, markers, arrows, and walls never overlap. Auto-turn endpoints also reserve\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:79:# - A solver can infer SEG_LEN by counting the mirrored tail and EXTRA_STEPS by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:80:#   counting the reverse-diagonal tail, then add them to get the total step budget.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:82:# - The wall-turn arrow always has a post-wall segment of length 4, so the AABB\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:83:#   striping is actually visible. A separate auto-turn arrow shows that turn timing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:87:# - Arrow colors are unique per grid and wall colors exclude arrow colors, so arrow +\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:89:# - Marker tails live on two diagonals behind the arrow, away from the ray path, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:90:#   the scene reads as \"arrow + two count cues + walls + output trace\" rather than a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:95:#   between the arrow color and the most recently inherited wall color, both visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:100:# - Assumption: for each arrow, the reverse-diagonal same-color run starting two cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:104:# - Assumption: wall colors do not equal any arrow color. Generator enforces this so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:123:def _is_arrow_pts(pts: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:131:def _arrow_dir_start_missing(pts: list[tuple[int, int]]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:154:def _arrow_points(start_r: int, start_c: int, dr: int, dc: int) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int]], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:165:def _tail_points(start_r: int, start_c: int, dr: int, dc: int, steps: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/15/code.py:234:    arrows: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/cod