share one color. The new solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/30/code.py:67:#    - Because one anchor color repeats across multiple quadrants and the two sprite types use different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/30/code.py:83:#    - Every destination marker color appears as a source anchor color, repeated anchors span multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:16:#     - objects stay the same as the base task: 3-cell L arrows plus static wall pixels/segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:19:#     - arrows are no longer independent: they fire from nearer-to-center source to farther-to-center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:28:#       - arrow A starts below-left of the center and points up-right, so it is visually closer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:30:#       - arrow B starts farther away in the top-left and points down-right toward the same crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:39:#       - compared with the base task, one tail is missing after the crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:47:#     - optionally add one extra later arrow with 0-2 static-wall bounces to keep the scene from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:51:#       code: `for start_col, pts in arrows`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:52:#       old assumption: arrow order is irrelevant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:53:#       fused impact: invalid. Rays now interact, so arrows must be sorted by center distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:70:#     - arrow L-shapes, static walls, and planned ray cells are kept disjoint and in-bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:71:#     - wall colors are chosen from colors not used by arrows, preventing same-co