) in arrow_set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:556:                \"pts\": arrow_pts,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:586:        \"arrow_count\": int(distance_meta[\"arrow_count\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:594:    arrow_colors = palette[:3]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:597:    pair = _mandatory_pair_distance_order(H, W, int(arrow_colors[0]), int(arrow_colors[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:600:    arrows, reserved_paths, used_dist2, min_start, min_dist2 = pair\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:606:    for arrow in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:607:        for r, c in arrow[\"pts\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:610:            grid[int(r), int(c)] = int(arrow[\"color\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:615:        extra = _plan_extra_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:618:            color=int(arrow_colors[2]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:627:            arrow, local_input, local_output, dist2 = extra\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:628:            for r, c in arrow[\"pts\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:629:                grid[int(r), int(c)] = int(arrow[\"color\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/6/code.py:630:            for wpxs, wcol in arrow.get(\"walls\", []):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/20/code.py:58:#    narrow, so the output reads as maroon spread through many triangles plus a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/12/code.py:49:#    - Repeated anchor colors across different quadrants show the same sprite type in multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/12/code.py:56:#    - For a healthy sample, at least one anchor color must appear in multiple quadrants and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/20/code.py:41:#    - Marker count is fixed to 3 so one sample can show multiple side codes without\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/20/code.py:67:#      can observe the same source sprite appearing in multiple orientations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/5/code.py:32:#      This ensures the output shows aligned heads plus uneven tails, which is the distinctive visual effect.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/5/code.py:51:#      the preserved-tail rule is visible in a few examples and cannot be mistaken for the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/5/code.py:151:# - The transformation collapses the staircase only at the head end; tail positions still encode each segment's input length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/5/code.py:165:    - Keep each segment's own original length when redrawing, so only the heads align while the tails remain uneven.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/26/code.py:44:#   multiple targets, preserving the original \"copy to several places\" structure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/1/code.py:20:#     each occupied slot contains a tiny 2-3 pixel marker anchored at the slot's top-left corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/1/code.py:37:#       an orange 3-pixel corner marker inside the frame does not map to any orange object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/1/code.py:44:#     gives the solver multiple confirmations that marker color is not the deciding factor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/1/code.py:46:#     marker color is reused by multiple source types. This blocks regression to the original color match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/1/code.py:53:#     every sprite contains a unique connected 2-3 pixel signature drawn from a small library.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/1/code.py:241:    - One background color, one gray rectangular frame, and sparse 2-3 pixel monochrome markers inside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/36/code.py:21:#    L-shaped trail between the two rectangles. The wallpaper itself changes from axial stripes to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/36/code.py:26:#    cases while still giving repeated support across multiple colored trajectories in each sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/14/code.py:48:#       diagonal chains that remain visually sparse without collapsing into multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/2/code.py:202:    - The background is the most common color. Each non-background 8-connected component has exactly 3 pixels and uses a 1+2 color split: one uniquely colored apex pixel plus two same-colored arm pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/2/code.py:208:    - If the landing cell lies on another sprite, recolor that entire hit sprite to maroon (9). If multiple projectiles land on the same empty background cell, paint that cell blue (1); otherwise a lone empty-cell landing becomes maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/28/code.py:49:#     so multiple disconnected segments may share a color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/28/code.py:158:    - Multiple segments may share a color, so color is not a unique identity cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1ae2feb7/12/code.py:33:#      cells can become colored if uniquely claimed or remain 0 if multiple bar periods coincide.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1ae2feb7/12/code.py:63:#    periodic dots, and the regular holes where multiple periods coincide. No invisible ordering by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/16/code.py:255:# === CFG: Sprite type and multiplicity ===\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e