75/10/code.py:39:#      multiple visual facings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:43:#      combo, only emitter recovery survives, and it must be replaced by arrow-template matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:51:#    - Generation precomputes all arrow placements whose 3 cells are in bounds, whose nearest edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:52:#      is unique, and whose tip+5*toward_edge destination is also in bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:55:#    - Under this toward-edge geometry, legal 5-step destinations stay in narrow border bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:61:#    - The crucial observable is disagreement between arrow facing and actual shot direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:63:#      arrow\" solver on the same input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:64:#    - Repeated support is added by forcing multiple misleading sprites and by mixing different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:65:#      arrow facings within at least one shared nearest-edge class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:69:#      recolor whole 3-pixel components. No extra overlays, legends, or multi-color coding are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:78:#    - For each sprite, compare `visual_dir` from the arrow template with `actual_dir` from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:84:#    - Every non-bg component is exactly one 3-pixel arrow matching a unique template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:85:#    - Every generated arrow has a unique nearest edge; ties are excluded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:86:#    - The projectile always starts from the arrow tip, not from any other pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:138:def _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:143:    for tip in comp:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:144:        tr, tc = tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:148:                matches.append((tip, direction))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:175:def _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:180:    tip_data = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:181:    if tip_data is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:183:    tip, _visual_dir = tip_data\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:188:    return tip, actual_dir\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:193:    Fire projectiles from 3-pixel arrow sprites, but aim them by border proximity instead of arrow facing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:197:    - Every non-background 8-connected component is a monochrome 3-pixel arrow in one of 8 visual facings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:198:    - The arrow tip still identifies the launch cell, but the arrow's pointing direction is not the movement rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:201:    - Match each component to an arrow template to recover its tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:202:    - Compare the sprite's occupied cells to the four grid edges; the projectile travels 5 cells from the tip TOWARD the uniquely nearest edge, always axis-aligned.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:204:    - If multiple projectiles land on the same empty background cell, paint it blue (1); otherwise a lone empty-background landing paints maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:206:    Key insight: The arrowhead is a red herring. Shape tells you where the shot starts, but the shot direction comes from the sprite's global position relative to the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:223:        td = _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(comp, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:267:        td = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:292:def _sprite_cells(tip: tuple[int, int], visual_dir: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:293:    tr, tc = tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:327:                    \"tip\": (tr, tc),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:429:        if _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(coords, H, W) is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/22/code.py:26:#    - Keep 2-3 movers so the asymmetric row rule repeats across multiple colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/6/code.py:20:#   the full centered object rather than leaving endpoint-side details behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:20:#      follows that continuation automatically. At a junction with multiple non-backtracking\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/25/code.py:415:    - At a junction with multiple forward continuations, the particle prefers alternating side branches: first eligible choice takes the left branch, next eligible choice takes the right branch, then left again, and so on. If the scheduled side branch does not exist, it keeps following the available corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:8:#    - Base task: each 3-pixel triangle encodes a direction, then \"teleports\" its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:23:#    - The board now contains two visually distinct object classes: 3-pixel triangles\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:72:#    - `_extract_objects()` assumes every non-bg component is either a 3-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/21/code.py:281:    - Non-bg objects are either 3-pixel triangle sprites (axis-aligned L or diagonal V)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/33/code.py:23:#    - When multiple movers overlap, stamping order is by visible sprite area:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/26/code.py:83:      - crop choice uses visible multiplicity, not color ids or interior-color arithmetic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/17/code.py:45:# - Keep 2-3 movers and 0-1 distractors as in the base task so the same fused rule repeats across multiple colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/30/code.py:56:#    Gap sizes remain in a narrow range so the board stays sparse and legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:354:        raise ValueError(\"grid too narrow for dependency corridor\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/6/code.py:10:#    - Combo: the frame interior is blank. Instead, single-cell markers sit in a narrow band left of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/6/code.py:28:#    - At least one source color spans multiple quadrant modes, so the fusion does not collapse into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/6/code.py:153:    - Just outside the frame, a narrow band on the left carries colored row markers and a narrow band\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/6/code.py:641:    assert cross_mode_sources > 0, \"expected at least one source color to span multiple quadrant modes\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:37:#      usually horizontal only: blank outer columns disappear, producing a narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:50:#    - To keep the change legible, generator columns come from two narrow but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:60:#      elsewhere. This avoids stacking multiple cue types into one crowded region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/3/code.py:41:# - Keep 2-3 movers and 0-1 distractors so the rule repeats across multiple colors without becoming crowded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/24/code.py:59:#    repeated terminal cycle phase of the lone trajectory, and multiple template\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/34/code.py:60:#     still fitting multiple frames inside the original 10-15 x 14-20 envelope.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/34/code.py:64:#     mover visibly replicates to multiple targets. This prevents the task from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/34/code.py:69:#     there are now multiple frames and the wide bottom frame can dominate the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/34/code.py:96:#       * multiple independent boxes on the right,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/34/code.py:237:    - Detect multiple frame rectangles on the right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/21/code.py:261:#    yields multiple sibling outputs and the marker count is always 3 or 4. Panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/21/code.py:354:    assert len(set(colors)) >= 2, \"marker colors must expose multiple cycle phases\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:20:#    becomes t=6..12 because it keeps length 7 and only slides so its tail lands at 12. Compared with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:21:#    the seed behavior, long tails are no longer cropped and the aligned side moves from \"both ends\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:22:#    to \"tail only\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:32:#    and the correct start position is derived from the shared reference tail ref_t1 and that redraw\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:38:#    the output keeps that long segment and only shifts it left/upstream to align the tail. Distinct\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:43:#    segments visibly grow until their tails meet the reference tail, and long segments visibly slide\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:45:#    the \"extend\" change and would weaken the evidence for tail-only alignment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:47:#    Outputs form neat flush tails with staggered heads, which is easy to parse by eye. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:149:    Align parallel colored segments so they all end at the reference tail, extending only the ones that are too short.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:162:    Key insight: The reference supplies a shared tail and a minimum required length. Short segments are completed backward to the reference span, while long segments keep their extra head instead of being cropped.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:63:#     This gives repeated evidence for recoloring across multiple movers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/28/code.py:46:#    - Wrong-length same-color segments make the size rule observable, while multiple distinct\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/14/code.py:50:#   - The same cavity size repeats multiple times and receives the same final recolored sprite, making the size rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/23/code.py:85:- the frame advertises multiple row and column marks for a color, but only the ordered diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/1/code.py:544:    \"\"\"Carve a narrow bg separator from the left edge without disconnecting path.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:26:#      legend entry, count the red sprite's 3 pixels, choose yellow from the count-3 entry,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:34:#      multiple placements supporting inference from a few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:60:#      This reduces clutter compared with mixing multiple legend styles around the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/24/code.py:36:  - The task is not simplified into a plain top/bottom sort: each side still needs multiple frames and repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/12/code.py:40:  markers replace some border cells and there are multiple frames. The combo solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/12/code.py:62:- Humans can directly see two independent clues: multiple frames, and border colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/12/code.py:139:    Stamp recolored sprites into multiple marked frames using edge-color coordinates and a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/12/code.py:211:            assert src_col not in source_to_frame, f\"source color {src_col} appears in multiple frames\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/32/code.py:74:# - No hidden numeric ordering is used. All evidence is spatial and repeated across multiple movers, which keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b0280bc/1/code.py:184:    - Every edge weight is the visible ribbon width (1..3 pixels), not its geometric length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:289:    Recolor particles as they thread through a narrow corridor, using alternating turn priority with a backup turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:298:    - Because the path is a narrow corridor, the particle keeps moving straight until the corridor wall blocks its next cell; that blocked wall cell is marked with the end color if it is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:323:    \"\"\"Reject local rooms so the path reads as a narrow 1-2 cell corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Build a single narrow serpentine corridor that guarantees an early fallback turn.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:388:    # At most one gentle width-2 bulge keeps the corridor visibly narrow instead of turning it into a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/33/code.py:219:    The output is not decided by a single pass. First everything snaps to the edge, then iterative sweeps resolve both same-group and cross-group rectangle collisions, which can push a frame multiple square-widths inward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/3/code.py:44:    - use 3-4 distinct cycle colors so one color can repeatedly mean left while multiple \"other\" colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/3/code.py:68:      by odd/even bend count, because the same blocker color causes the same turn orientation in multiple places\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/21/code.py:16:#    parse from only a few ARC examples. Placeholders repeat colors inside the frame so every source color has multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/1/code.py:48:  - Generator examples keep multiple objects in each half and deliberately create overlap cases on both sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/32/code.py:247:            raise ValueError(f\"Expected one control pixel in {half} half, found multiple\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/25/code.py:46:#    The key ambiguity risk is having multiple columns share the same shape class\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:32:#      tip, first finds a Down launch, later takes a longer Down branch over a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:40:#    legible: humans can see one marker, several restart tips on the boundary,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:56:#      round before side branches are tested. Those boundary tips are what allow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/11/code.py:70:#    relaunchs produce multiple spatially separated painted rounds even though\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/4/code.py:37:#      frame from overlapping multiple edge frames on the same side, keeping the solver's anchor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/19/code.py:39:#    - D9 splitting multiplies output width, so every source frame is forced to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/19/code.py:80:#      different frames because multiple source colors from different frames share\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/19/code.py:94:#      multiple legends can share the same target, and those source colors, even\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/19/code.py:350:            assert col not in color_to_frame, f\"placeholder color {col} appears in multiple frames\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/25/code.py:63:#    A human can compare multiple examples and see that position relative to the cuts controls both whether\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/25/code.py:66:#    No cell carries multiple semantics: bg, ctrl ray, stationary split-line fg, moved-region color, or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/4/code.py:27:      visible tail from row 10 to row 17\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/4/code.py:33:  - keep the sprite centered with margin >= 4, which guarantees a visible far-side ctrl tail after the sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/4/code.py:54:  - every active line shows both parts of the combo: overwritten interior fg and a ctrl tail beyond the sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/14/code.py:72:# - The generator rejects samples unless stage 1 creates multiple fg pixels on c2, stage 2 creates fg on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:21:#   - Width is restricted to the small visible set {2, 3}; that is narrow enough\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:33:#     non-background population. The generator keeps the narrow band dominant over\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:481:    \"\"\"Stable 15x15 narrow-band layout with a readable left-edge separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:3:# Name: 符号转向指令+箭头标记+模板方向符号\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:22:# - Replace the old single-pixel sources with 3-cell arrowheads in the first cycle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:23:#   color. The arrow tip is the launch cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:27:# - Fusion choice for the D4/D11 tension: every arrowhead must point in the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:30:#   `v` arrowheads, motion starts downward; if the turn bars read [L,R,R], later\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:36:# - The added symbols all use low-cardinality, human-visible geometry: arrow shape,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:42:#   the hypothesis space while still leaving multiple examples across the dataset\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:46:#   replaced by 8-connected size-3 arrowhead decoding.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:48:#   new symbolic cues, so the solver now decodes the arrowheads and template glyph\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:60:# - Arrowheads are placed only on ambient path cells, with the tip's forward cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:65:#   the paint cycle, side bars are the turn sequence, and the arrow/glyph direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:73:#   glyph stay in the top-left template region, while arrowheads stay inside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:81:#   has exactly one indicator, the glyph direction matches every arrow marker, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:82:#   all placed arrows are non-degenerate against legacy neighbor-priority launch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:106:def _arrow_cells(tip_r: int, tip_c: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:108:        (int(tip_r + dr), int(tip_c + dc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:113:def _decode_arrow_component(coords: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int, str] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:119:        for tip_r, tip_c in comp:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:120:            if set(_arrow_cells(int(tip_r), int(tip_c), direction)) == comp:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:121:                matches.append((int(tip_r), int(tip_c), direction))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:157:        f\"arrow direction {marker_dir} must agree with template glyph {global_dir}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:162:def _find_arrow_markers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:170:        decoded = _decode_arrow_component(coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:173:        tip_r, tip_c, direction = decoded\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:175:        nr, nc = int(tip_r + dr), int(tip_c + dc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:177:            f\"marker tip at ({tip_r},{tip_c}) points {direction} out of bounds\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/c