 present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/25/code.py:234:    blue-region outlier,\" while the marker has narrowed from an unrestricted\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/28/code.py:13:#    1-pixel L-shaped trail colored with that object's dominant fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/28/code.py:17:#    real many-to-many assignment over multiple corners rather than a single match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/28/code.py:32:#    internal holes, so the board stays readable even with multiple objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/10/code.py:24:#       multiple groups so the recolor rule is inferable rather than a one-off coincidence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/10/code.py:52:#     - Every chosen source color reappears in multiple groups, making the source->target color map visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/21/code.py:56:- The core keeps multiple interior pattern colors, but the outer border of the core stays fill-colored so the missing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/21/code.py:85:- There is only one internal object, one outer frame, and one sparse noise side. No region mixes multiple annotation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/37/code.py:38:#      there are multiple true objects plus distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/37/code.py:68:# - Opposite frame sides share colors, so each true object has multiple color-valid candidate corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:47:#    - The center object visibly has an L-shaped dense region, not a plain rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/19/code.py:17:#      twice: there are multiple true sources, and some non-source rectangles can be comparable or larger.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/19/code.py:27:#    - Old object extraction assumed a single largest interior component; this breaks with multiple true sources and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/26/code.py:310:    - A small black-and-blue board contains one or more large blue regions, several detached black defects inside blue, and sometimes a black leaf tip attached to a larger black mass.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/26/code.py:457:    \"\"\"Blue cells that would become single-pixel leaf tips on large black regions.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/26/code.py:481:    \"\"\"Optionally place a small number of large-component leaf tips.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/11/code.py:29:#   single L-shaped leftover region. A sprite lying above or below the template is mirrored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/24/code.py:57:  Original solver would read \"multiple reds on one row\" and try a horizontal mirror.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/10/code.py:22:#    multiple matching dihedral transforms, and always places 1-2 distractors. One distractor is biased to be at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/17/code.py:41:#      fused rule instead preserves the whole grid and applies multiple copy operations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/6/code.py:63:#      any sample with zero or multiple matches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/27/code.py:31:#    - Keep 2-9 defects of size 1-3 so samples show repetition and multiple sizes, but avoid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/27/code.py:32:#      extra target classes such as leaf tips that would muddy the fused rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/27/code.py:105:      spurs to absorb and no separate leaf-tip target class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/19/code.py:28:#      - D7/2 contributes the disambiguation rule \"when multiple candidate colors are present,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/19/code.py:35:#      so the color ordering is evidenced multiple times.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/19/code.py:41:#      once one marker component may contain multiple payload colors, because same-color distractors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:32:#    L-shaped core canvas -> erase the dominant non-background fill color to 0. The result is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/5/code.py:85:#      colors and positions inside one size group, multiple examples visibly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/38/code.py:32:#    - Only two pattern colors are used, and both are repeated multiple times, so the post-crop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/8/code.py:26:#    orange ring + black center; now it stays plain black. A 1-pixel black tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/8/code.py:28:#    tip itself becomes red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/8/code.py:44:#    multiple small black holes that stay unmarked and one or more red-centered\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/23/code.py:78:- Multiple disconnected destination frames are immediately visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/14/code.py:35:#    - \"holes can be found anywhere inside the bbox\" is narrowed to rectangular bg\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:44:#      narrows the target to the two blue-striped holes. One hole shows a red\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:51:#    - D1 must matter: at least one size group contains multiple edge cue colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:53:#    - D3 must matter: at least one (h, w, cue) group contains multiple distinct\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:82:#    The same size appears with multiple cues, and the same cue appears with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:83:#    multiple marker signatures, so each reasoning layer has repeated support.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/7/code.py:29:- Each template has multiple disconnected frames, so the D3 change is also always visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/7/code.py:60:- Repeated rectangle sizes appear in multiple places, making the grouping cues necessary rather than decorative.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/3/code.py:138:    Chain a single seed payload through multiple full red separator lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/24/code.py:62:#    Across 2-4 examples, a solver can see that \"tiny isolated holes\" and \"tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/24/code.py:75:#    tips attached to larger black regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/24/code.py:270:    - Blue (1) foreground regions sit against black (0) regions, with a few tiny black holes embedded inside blue and a few black leaf tips protruding from larger black masses.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/24/code.py:275:    - Next detect two anomaly types in the cleaned grid: every black 4-connected component of size <= 3 is an internal defect, and every pixel of a larger black component with black 4-degree <= 1 is a leaf tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/24/code.py:276:    - Paint a Chebyshev-1 halo around each anomaly, but only on cells that are blue in the cleaned grid: internal defects use orange (7), leaf tips use magenta (6), and every anomaly center itself becomes red (2).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/24/code.py:279:    - The puzzle still hinges on distinguishing detached tiny black holes from dangling black tips, but the output now encodes both the anomaly type and the blue-region boundary: the center is always red, while the surrounding ring both changes color by type and is clipped to the blue area.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/24/code.py:444:    \"\"\"Place 1-3 single-pixel leaf tips on large black-region boundaries.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/12/code.py:125:    - Within each size group, first match by the number of black marker pixels; whenever that still leaves multiple candidates, resolve the tie by comparing the marker-coordinate pattern inside the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/12/code.py:127:    Key insight: The puzzle is solved by a genuine two-step cue hierarchy: size only says which pieces can fit, marker count narrows the candidate slot set, and the marker layout inside equally counted rectangles determines the final correspondence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/17/code.py:73:- The multiple destination frames are directly visible, and the output crop keeps the bg gaps between them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/17/code.py:96:- Assumption: exactly one color pair forms multiple large hole-bearing components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/17/code.py:249:    - Recover the two structural colors by finding the color pair whose union forms multiple disconnected hole-bearing frames, then crop the union bbox of the whole arrangement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/16/code.py:81:      the cavity has multiple independent islands, so sprites must be assigned to a hole group before\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/16/code.py:217:            tail = assign_groups(next_remaining, order_idx + 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/16/code.py:218:            if tail is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/16/code.py:219:                placement.update(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/16/code.py:368:    tail = slack - lead\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/16/code.py:376:    if tail < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/10/code.py:51:#      a large black region, so they become legal degree-1 tips after conversion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/33/code.py:281:      may have one-cell leaf tips protruding into adjacent blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/15/code.py:202:    - Small black holes or thin black leaf tips sit inside the blue structures.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/34/code.py:274:    - The output is no longer driven by tiny black anomalies or leaf tips. It is driven by depth:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/23/code.py:391:    - Blue regions may contain tiny enclosed anomalies of several colors: black, red (2), or gray (5); large black regions may also contribute 1-cell leaf tips into blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/23/code.py:549:    \"\"\"Place a few black leaf tips from large black components into blue.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/1/code.py:52:#    - Leaf detection assumes large black components can contain degree-0/1 tips; the generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/1/code.py:65:#      and magenta appears only around boundary tips while orange stays around internal holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/1/code.py:71:#      visible in the input: isolated internal holes vs tips sticking out of a large black mass.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/1/code.py:147:    - Blue areas may contain tiny black internal defects, and large black regions may poke 1-cell leaf tips into blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/1/code.py:155:    Key insight: The puzzle still isolates structural black irregularities, but the output now encodes both geometry and defect type: isolated holes get orange crosses, boundary tips get magenta crosses.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:39:#    - Large black regions still contribute marked leaf tips when they stick one cell into blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:40:#      That keeps the structural contrast between \"isolated small black in grey\" and \"tip of a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:55:#    - Original leaf detection assumed any degree-0/1 pixel in a large black component was a tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:78:#      grey-around-black means \"mark\", black-around-grey means \"absorb\", blue next to a black tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:79:#      means the tip is a protrusion target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:84:#    - `main()` assumes small marked defects are strictly grey-enclosed and leaf tips are blue-adjacent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:189:    Mark grey-enclosed black defects and black leaf tips, while absorbing grey noise in black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:194:      sprout one-pixel black leaf tips into it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/38/code.py:46:#      stops placing leaf protrusions so that no unmarked branch tips compete with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/22/code.py:85:#    - `main()` assumes size buckets are meaningful even when multiple targets exist. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/3/code.py:49:#      flipped they become degree-1 tips of a large black component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/3/code.py:176:    - Large black regions may also have thin leaf-like black tips poking into blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/3/code.py:413:    \"\"\"Place degree-1 black tips, preferring heavily clipped locations.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/3/code.py:522:    # Demand multiple black-blocked halo arms so the blue-only clipping is obvious\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/22/code.py:43:       cue is the L shape, while the transformation is still diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/22/code.py:56:     set was invalid. That fails once L shapes become meaningful.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/22/code.py:75:     compare \"row/col line -> orthogonal mirror\" against \"L shape -> diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/36/code.py:26:#    black cells. Example on a narrow black stripe:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/36/code.py:31:#    On a 10-13 cell board, this can split a black stripe into multiple pieces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/36/code.py:62:#    black tips, making the growth step visibly relevant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/36/code.py:65:#    existing halo or where multiple spur footprints touch. This keeps the board\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/36/code.py:316:    - Small black defects sit inside blue regions, and large black regions may have leaf-like black tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/40/code.py:70:#    The generator rejects samples unless they contain multiple blue spurs, multiple non-blue noise\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/15/code.py:85:    - Repeating blocked reflections in multiple groups makes the \"only move into empty space\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/35/code.py:43:#      around all four black cells rather than only its tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/28/code.py:142:def _target_details(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/28/code.py:235:    preserve, _ = _target_details(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/28/code.py:521:    _, stats = _target_details(absorbed, connectivity=8, boundary_only_small=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/16/code.py:42:#    is harmless. That breaks for 2-3 pixel defects because internal overlap within\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/16/code.py:201:    Mark black anomalies in compact blue regions, but cancel any halo cells shared by multiple defects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/16/code.py:205:    - Some larger black regions may contribute single-pixel leaf tips into blue, and black areas may also contain thin blue spur pixels that should be absorbed before marking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/16/code.py:381:    \"\"\"Optionally add 0-1 leaf tips from a large black region into blue.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/6/code.py:152:      may have single-pixel leaf tips extending into blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/8/code.py:22:#   2 or 3 pixels. Gap 2 means one stamp-step; gap 3 means two stamp-steps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/8/code.py:309:      locally: 2 pixels -> 1 stamp-step, 3 pixels -> 2 stamp-steps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/6/code.py:33:  A 2-colored sprite next to an isolated 3-pixel is point-reflected, but the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/6/code.py:94:- Every mapped color appears multiple times: in the legend and in at least one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/37/code.py:260:    - Defects can be singleton holes, 2-cell holes, 3-cell holes, or leaf tips of larger black components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/13/code.py:44:#    - Only two structural target categories remain: tiny isolated black holes and leaf tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/13/code.py:187:      1-pixel leaf tips protruding into adjacent blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:41:#      only the tip attached to a black mass is.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:78:#      interior black holes inside blue are left untouched, while black tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:87:#      original task's clean region structure and makes the protruding tips easy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:93:#      one-cell black boundary tips are highlighted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:284:    Highlight only boundary-attached one-pixel black tips in blue regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:292:      blue, and one-cell protruding tips attached to larger black regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:304:    pixel must be the exposed one-cell tip of a larger black structure, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:32:#    output dot; a one-cell black tip jutting into blue remains black and gets a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:40:#    orange halos around internal defects, magenta halos around leaf tips, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:50:#    it can paint internal defects orange and leaf tips magenta, then restore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:55:#    regions. Leaf tips are inserted only on blue cells adjacent to exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:64:#    leaf tips attached to large black masses; isolated input specks of several\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:288:    - Large blue (1) and black (0) regions tile the board, with a few tiny black defects fully embedded in blue and a few black leaf tips sticking out from larger black regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:293:    - On that cleaned black mask, classify every black 4-connected component of size <= 3 as an internal defect, and every pixel of a larger black component with black 4-degree <= 1 as a leaf tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:294:    - Paint a Chebyshev-1 halo around each anomaly: internal defects use orange (7), leaf tips use magenta (6), anomaly centers stay black, and the detected spur pixels themselves are rendered as magenta singletons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:297:    - The task still depends on reconstructing the black geometry before classifying anomalies, but now two distinct magenta motifs coexist: isolated foreign-color specks inside black regions become standalone magenta dots, while black leaf tips attached to large regions get magenta rings around black centers; tiny detached black defects are the only anomalies with orange rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:440:    \"\"\"Find blue cells that can become one-step leaf tips of large black components.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:467:    \"\"\"Place 1-3 single-pixel black leaf tips on large black-region boundaries.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/9/code.py:59:  - The canvas now shows multiple isolated color-4 pixels. In the output, only the chosen marker per legend disappears under a composite; the decoys remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/9/code.py:362:    - The canvas background contains multiple color-4 marker pixels: one true anchor marker per legend plus 1-2 decoys.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/24/code.py:223:    - Keep only in-bounds stamped pixels; the origin copy is recolored to `O`, and any multiply covered cells are also recolored to `O`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/9/code.py:34:#      leaf tips of large black components, and absorbable blue spurs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/9/code.py:51:#    - Every sample contains multiple ordinary defects plus at least one leaf, so both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/9/code.py:196:      regions can have single-pixel leaf tips poking into blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/7/code.py:52:#    - Generator always places multiple spurs and multiple grey noise dots, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:32:       an L-shaped red marker. Its corner is the anchor, and the payload reflects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:96:     multiple overlapping chains.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:481:    - L-shaped red marker -> diagonal reflection\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/16/code.py:15:#       - If an orbit already contains multiple payload cells, the copies generated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/16/code.py:43:#       capture unrelated same-color pixels. That is unsafe once multiple copies can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/16/code.py:67:#     - Payload cells lie on a narrow ring around the cross, so the local geometry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/10/code.py:456:            tail_pad = grid_h - (marker_r0 + MARKER_PANEL_HEIGHT)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/10/code.py:457:            if tail_pad < BOTTOM_PAD_MIN:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:63:# - All translated copy anchors remain integer multiples of (h, w), so every copy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/6/code.py:324:    - Place the finished composite on the canvas using the anchor position encoded by the marker square's inner 3x3 pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:67:# - All stamp anchors differ by integer multiples of the common 4x4 box size,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/17/code.py:62:# - Original placement math using multiples of template height/width still holds because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/19/code.py:68:    - Recolor the origin copy to `B/O`, and recolor any multiply covered cells to `B/O` as well.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/2/code.py:21:#      uniformly spaced. Adjacent visible gaps are only 2 or 3 pixels, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/2/code.py:25:#      (h, w), so neighboring copies share a strip. Multiply covered cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/2/code.py:90:#    - Non-uniform source is enforced by requiring both 2-pixel and 3-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/2/code.py:278:    - Singleton rows and columns are warped rather than uniform: each adjacent visible gap is either 2 or 3 pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/26/code.py:644:        narrowed = [c for c in subset if score_fn(c) == best]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/26/code.py:645:        if narrowed:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/26/code.py:646:            subset = narrowed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/10/code.py:321:    - The singleton scaffold is not evenly spaced: sorted neighboring rows/cols differ by 2 or 3 pixels, and the singleton ranks form an 8-connected coarse shape with diagonal-only contacts allowed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:185:def _narrow_vertical_corridor(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:432:        if not _narrow_vertical_corridor(grid, jc, top1, jr, child_n, min_open_steps=5):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:435:        if not _narrow_vertical_corridor(grid, right_root[1], top2, jr, child_n, min_open_steps=6):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/19/code.py:53:#    - Original \"anchor is one interior pixel in the 3x3 square\" is invalid because multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/5/code.py:30:#    - Every generated frame uses both 8 and 9 multiple times, so the local mirror rule is not a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/7/code.py:46:#      uniquely identifiable by connectivity while avoiding multiple competing high-degree nodes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/7/code.py:59:#      become longer L-shaped paths; parity would create fake nodes on the arms. The fused solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/7/code.py:261:    - Recolor the origin copy to `O`, and recolor any multiply covered filled pixel to `O` as well.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/4/code.py:296:    - Place each enlarged composite by the anchor marker. If multiple composites cover the same output pixels, the earlier legend in reading order is the front layer and every shared pixel is recolored to that front legend's frame color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/2/code.py:55:#   multiple legends, but the generator emits one counted legend per sample so the fusion does not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/28/code.py:67:#    - The legend still uses one narrow column block per side, so symbols remain easy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/27/code.py:81:     multiple direction sectors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:34:#      target. If a choke narrows below 6, the mover stops at the farthest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:74:#    - Big mover sizes 5..7 make narrow gates visibly narrower than the mover.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:84:#      large mover footprint interacting with visibly narrow chokepoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:308:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, max(1, n - 2))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:309:    remove = int(n - narrow_w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/32/code.py:42:#   are flush and all of them emit, so the fused rule is supported multiple times.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/1/code.py:85:# - Repetition exists along both dimensions of change: multiple examples can show several mouths,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:33:#   - The object vocabulary stays small: closed shell emitters, one L-shaped blocker, and at most no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/15/code.py:69:#   red/blue diagonals while narrow-hole examples produce dashed red diagonals, and both kinds stop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/8/code.py:23:#      So multiple color-4 pixels may appear at once.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/8/code.py:46:#    - Old position decoding assumed a unique marker pixel; invalid once multiple bits are on.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/24/code.py:46:#   removed, multiple legends would require a new composition rule between several\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/2/code.py:69:#    mapping, and multiple emitters with different colors provide cross-example\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:32:#       the last gravity-reachable placement above the first too-narrow slice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:66:#       the last shaft becomes narrower row by row. In blocked examples the mover stops just above\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:67:#       the narrow segment while the red square remains below it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:77:#       gravity-like descent plus a monotone narrowing that eventually becomes too tight.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:226:      too narrow for the square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:396:        \"tail_r\": int(shelf2_r),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:397:        \"tail_c\": int(drop2_c),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:402:def _choose_taper_plan(grid: np.ndarray, tail_r: int, tail_c: int, n: int, reached: bool) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:405:    body_len = int(dest_r - tail_r)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:410:    room_left = int(tail_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:411:    room_right = int(w - (tail_c + n))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:529:    plan = _choose_taper_plan(grid, int(taper[\"tail_r\"]), int(taper[\"tail_c\"]), n, reached)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:534:        int(taper[\"tail_r\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:535:        int(taper[\"tail_c\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/25/code.py:56:# - The original uniqueness assert on trigger rows is too strong once more holes are allowed; multiple holes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/35/code.py:192:    - A full-height grey (5) separator splits the grid into a wide left pane and a narrow right pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:71:#     The corridor/background inversion is inferable from large-area corners vs narrow strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:319:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:320:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:38:#   - main() now assumes a narrow-left / wide-right layout. The generator guarantees\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:57:#     pane, and outputs that are narrower than inputs because only the right pane is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:113:    - A full-height grey (5) separator sits near the left edge, leaving a narrow sprite pane on the left and a much wider empty pane on the right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:132:        f\"expected narrow-left / wide-right panes, got left_w={sep}, right_w={right_w}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/23/code.py:19:#      gaps are either 2 or 3 pixels, encoding 1 or 2 stamp steps respectively\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/23/code.py:130:    - 