, not a new hidden semantic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/3/code.py:60:- The original code assumed a single corridor, so it never had to reason about multiple routes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/12/code.py:96:#       This keeps the inference space narrow enough for ARC-style reasoning.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:281:def _solve_details(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:332:    - If the current target is blocked by a too-narrow branch, the mover stops at the reachable placement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:335:    return _solve_details(np.array(grid, dtype=int))[\"out\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:375:    details = _solve_details(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:378:    if details[\"reached_count\"] < len(details[\"targets\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:379:        blocked_idx = int(details[\"reached_count\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:382:        \"target_count\": len(details[\"targets\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:384:        \"ordered_reached_count\": int(details[\"reached_count\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:387:        \"final_pos\": details[\"final_pos\"],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:451:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:452:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:575:        details = _solve_details(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:580:    if not np.array_equal(out, details[\"out\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:587:        if not np.array_equal(details[\"final_pos\"], target_positions[-1]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/20/code.py:50:       * multiple barrier crossings with alternating gap heights,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:81:# (tip_width, short_arm_len, long_arm_len, long_arm_thickness)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:117:    tip_width: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:130:        c0 = w - tip_width\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:131:    mask[:short_arm_len, c0 : c0 + tip_width] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:215:    tip_width, short_arm_len, long_arm_len, long_arm_thickness = params\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:216:    base = _build_up_l_mask(tip_width, short_arm_len, long_arm_len, long_arm_thickness, handed)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:341:    Build a red cascade by activating L-shaped blue blobs whose short arm end is a hidden port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:349:    - Each activated blob launches a ray from its uniquely narrowest extreme side, with width 1 or 2 from that side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:352:    Key insight: The firing side is encoded by geometry alone: the short arm tip of each L-shape is the only extreme edge with length 1-2, so its direction and ray thickness can be inferred from the silhouette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:401:    # --- STEP 3) Extract blue blobs and infer each hidden port from its L-shaped silhouette ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:432:        \"\"\"Recolor a blob to red when first hit; enqueue it to emit from its hidden short-arm tip.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:455:        \"\"\"Extend a thick ray from the inferred short-arm tip until boundary or another blob hit.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/37/code.py:74:   - The blue route is a sparse diagonal ribbon. Reflectors are outside the ribbon, so no cell carries multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/11/code.py:70:   - Junctions are sparse and separated; targets sit at branch tips instead of cluttering the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:26:     2. One extra same-colored tip pixel sticks out on one side of that L body. The tip is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:28:     3. The destination is a red docking frame whose inner cavity is an L-shaped blue notch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:33:        at the farthest reachable placement. The tip disappears in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:40:     * If the tip points right, the start placement must have exactly one feasible neighbor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:46:   - Only one body family is used: L shapes. This keeps the category count low while still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:55:   - \"Both key objects are solid squares\" is false. The mover is an L plus a tip, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:58:     colors, so the solver must detect the arrow-marked L component and the dock structurally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:63:     component (body plus tip) but only paint the L body at the terminal position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:69:     making the tip direction unambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:77:   - Humans can see three simultaneous cues: the mover is the irregular object with a tip, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:79:     the notch shape. The tip shows the initial slide direction without relying on color order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:85:   - The tip is a single pixel on existing river, so it does not clutter the scene.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:96:   - Exactly one non-river component is an L body plus exactly one side tip pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:259:def _find_arrow_l_info(comp: dict) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:265:    for tip_r, tip_c in coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:266:        body = coords - {(tip_r, tip_c)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:282:            if tip_r == r0 - 1 and c0 <= tip_c <= c1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:284:            elif tip_r == r1 + 1 and c0 <= tip_c <= c1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:286:            elif tip_c == c0 - 1 and r0 <= tip_r <= r1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:288:            elif tip_c == c1 + 1 and r0 <= tip_r <= r1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:292:            if not any((tip_r + dr, tip_c + dc) in body for dr, dc in _DIR4.values()):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:302:                    \"tip\": (int(tip_r), int(tip_c)),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:371:        info = _find_arrow_l_info(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:656:def _choose_tip_cell(grid: np.ndarray, r0: int, c0: int, coords, direction: str):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:812:    tip = _choose_tip_cell(grid, int(mover_anchor[0]), int(mover_anchor[1]), config[\"coords\"], start_dirs[0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:813:    if tip is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:818:    grid[int(tip[0]), int(tip[1])] = int(mover_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/co