y:22:     the same rotated L shape, and the frame opens toward the corridor only along the side where that L touches the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:58:   - The blue corridor is rendered as the union of translated copies of the same L shape, so every intended anchor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:67:     1. the mover is visibly L-shaped rather than square;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:69:     3. the red goal is a larger docking frame with an L-shaped blue notch, and reachable outputs keep that frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/12/code.py:35:#      narrow (2-4 rows) just like the original right receiving pane stayed narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/12/code.py:39:#      * multiple disjoint objects per grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/13/code.py:204:    - One full-height grey (5) separator column splits the grid into a left sprite field and a narrow right chamber.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:46:#   L-shaped path whose vertical leg length equals the hole height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:78:#   and the red signal is no longer a set of full-width rows but an L-shaped trace hugging the divider.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:81:# - The generator rejects layouts where multiple emitters all have the same height when there is room for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:87:#   stays legible even when multiple emitters contribute nearby L-shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:201:    - A full-height grey (5) separator column splits a narrow left ray pane from a wider right sprite pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/6/code.py:146:    - A full-height grey (5) separator column divides the grid into a wide left sprite pane and a narrow right ray pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/19/code.py:35:#   - Trigger rows are deduplicated with a set because multiple candidate rows can arise from one recess.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/28/code.py:32:#   multiple rectangles per band so the color-swap rule has repeated evidence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/28/code.py:44:#     minorities <= 3 pixels, so one color remains strictly most frequent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/41/code.py:53:#   is supported by multiple examples inside one grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/34/code.py:55:#   - Output never stacks multiple ray colors in the same row because row bands are disjoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/32/code.py:39:#   some rectangles disappear, the remaining ones split into multiple columns,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/36/code.py:171:    - A single full-height grey separator column splits the grid into a wider left pane and a narrow right pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/23/code.py:33:# - The right pane is narrowed only slightly less than the seed task: width is kept in 3..4.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:164:        raise AssertionError(\"vertical cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:183:    raise AssertionError(\"horizontal cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:188:    Build a red ray network by activating single-axis cross blobs whose narrowest arm is a hidden port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:196:    - The activated cross then emits a ray from the uniquely narrowest arm tip, with width 1 or 2 depending on that arm.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:199:    Key insight: Direction is encoded geometrically, not by color. The only arm end that is strictly narrower than the other three extremes is the implicit launch port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:305:        \"\"\"Extend a ray from each tip pixel until boundary or the first blob hit in that lane.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:334:# - a constant narrow top arm (width 1 or 2),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/4/code.py:168:    tail_ok = np.all(out[r, sep + 2 :] == bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/4/code.py:169:    return bool(marker_ok and tail_ok)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/6/code.py:50:#   fully connected 4x4 patch, even though it uses multiple colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/23/code.py:90:   - Because multiple differently colored frames appear on multiple non-zero input\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/29/code.py:73:- The generator reuses colors within a semantic column across multiple objects,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/12/code.py:53:#    Because each layer appears multiple times in every grid, the learner gets repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/10/code.py:63:#    In the output the near group stays flat, the middle group becomes tall/narrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/10/code.py:66:#    is supported by multiple instances rather than a one-off anomaly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/16/code.py:106:- To keep that sequence inferable, generator uses multiple body colors per class and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/21/code.py:104:   - Because each sample contains multiple frame orientations and at least one solid, a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/44/code.py:157:    - Right column: objects whose outer border contains multiple colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/21/code.py:85:#   stripes, so no region mixes multiple object types in a hard-to-parse way.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/4/code.py:74:#    multiple side-by-side stacks by dominant color, and within each stack the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/1/code.py:62:# - Humans can see multiple identical bottom launchers, so the multi-source\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/1/code.py:99:#   generator guarantees no blob spans multiple start columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/2/code.py:38:    noise:       one 3-cell L shape in the middle corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/2/code.py:88:    Right column: outer border contains multiple colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/39/code.py:238:    - Same colors may appear across multiple objects and across both kept categories.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/19/code.py:48:#    infer because both bands repeat multiple times and the original rectangle colors disappear completely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/19/code.py:60:#    clarity it is best if there are exactly two non-empty db groups and each group has multiple rectangles. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/26/code.py:50:#    The palette is small and visually ordered; each sample contains multiple objects per type; and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:28:#    a single memorized picture, but the family stays narrow enough to remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:31:#    The original solver logic already supports multiple ports per blob because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:34:#    uses that latent capability for the center blob, so BFS over multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:50:#    narrower and top-cropped relative to the input. A human can therefore infer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/7/code.py:88:- Only two rectangle colors are used per sample, and both repeat multiple times. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/5/code.py:146:    Right column: objects whose border contains multiple colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/33/code.py:38:    plus one detached L-shaped noise blob elsewhere\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/3/code.py:59:     multiple differently colored frames provide repeated evidence that all\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/36/code.py:51:       multiples of 4, and each column uses width 5 because the largest object is 5x5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/45/code.py:121:   - Since multiple different input frame colors map to the same output frame color, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/32/code.py:33:    - right-column class: border uses multiple colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/32/code.py:63:  classes repeat multiple times per sample (2..4 objects each).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/19/code.py:74:#    - A human sees a branching root with multiple green exits, two activated side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/3/code.py:51:#    Each sample includes multiple minority and multiple pure rectangles, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/3/code.py:252:        tail = (int(rect[\"ab\"]), int(rect[\"ar\"]), *tuple(map(int, rect[\"box\"])))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/3/code.py:254:            return (int(rect[\"db\"]), int(rect[\"dr\"]), *tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/3/code.py:256:            return (int(rect[\"area\"]), *tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/3/code.py:258:            return (int(rect[\"priority\"]), int(rect[\"db\"]), int(rect[\"dr\"]), *tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/3/code.py:260:            return (int(rect[\"priority\"]), int(rect[\"area\"]), *tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/27/code.py:75:  reasoning space narrow and readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/27/code.py:107:- The only color-related change is multiplicity: repeated colors across shapes are deliberate and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/31/code.py:29:     - outer border has multiple non-bg colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/31/code.py:109:  - among valid ones, left if border is one color, right if border uses multiple colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/4/code.py:48:#      branches. The key visible difference is \"one vertical ray lights multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/4/code.py:87:#    - A human can infer D6 by comparing that the same upward red line turns multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/47/code.py:78:  Status here: invalid. Objects are rectangles with multiple possible non-square sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/6/code.py:64:#   tied to visible cascade depth and repeated across multiple samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/13/code.py:31:#         1) there are multiple independent sources;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/13/code.py:42:#    - A generator that forbids ray-ray overlap is no longer valid, because multiple center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/13/code.py:59:#    - Active branch count is capped so the result stays legible even with multiple sources.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:17:#     edges. Its yellow cap sits one step diagonally inward from the segment's inner tip, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:45:#     both vertical and horizontal boundary segments, identify the inner tip, and test only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:48:#     because a corner green cell can touch blue from multiple offsets. The solver therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:70:#     non-segment cell on one of the two inward diagonals from its inner tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:375:            tip: tuple[int, int] | None = None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:383:                    tip = (int(r0), int(c0))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:387:                    tip = (int(r1), int(c0))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:394:                    tip = (int(r0), int(c1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:398:                    tip = (int(r0), int(c0))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:401:            if seg_cells is None or tip is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:406:                rr = int(tip[0] + d[0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:407:                cc = int(tip[1] + d[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:469:      placed one step diagonally inward from that segment's inner tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:734:        tip_r, tip_c = H - start_h, lane\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:735:        start_seg = [(int(r), int(lane)) for r in range(int(tip_r), H)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:739:        tip_r, tip_c = start_h - 1, lane\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:740:        start_seg = [(int(r), int(lane)) for r in range(0, int(tip_r) + 1)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:744:        tip_r, tip_c = lane, start_h - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:745:        start_seg = [(int(lane), int(c)) for c in range(0, int(tip_c) + 1)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:749:        tip_r, tip_c = lane, W - start_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:750:        start_seg = [(int(lane), int(c)) for c in range(int(tip_c), W)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:752:    cap_r = int(tip_r + start_dir[0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/2/code.py:753:    cap_c = int(tip_c + start_dir[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:5:# Name: 螺旋射线+箭头形起始标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:20:#    - New start object: a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite. Four red body pixels make the shaft/wedge and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:21:#      one yellow pixel protrudes on the firing side. The arrow tail is anchored on the boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:22:#      opposite the firing direction, so the protruding yellow tip is the visible cue for the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:29:#    - Example sketch: if a right-pointing arrow starts near the left edge, the first leg goes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:35:#    - Direction freedom is limited to the four cardinals and one arrow family, so the start cue is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:44:#      above it. That is false now, so start detection must match the arrow geometry instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:51:#    - New solver assumption: exactly one arrow exists; its red body has area 4; it has exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:52:#      non-red 4-neighbor tip; the full 5-cell shape matches one of four templates; and the tail is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:55:#    - Objects are still placed output-first. The generator paints the arrow, then for each active\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:62:#    - The arrow makes the initial direction visible without reading color ids. Horizontal starts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:75:#      yellow start tip, azure background. The new inference burden is geometric only:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:76:#      \"read direction from the arrow, then follow repeated clockwise turns.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:95:# --- Start arrow ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:100:        \"tip\": (0, 1),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:101:        \"tail\": (2, 1),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:105:        \"tip\": (2, 1),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:106:        \"tail\": (0, 1),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:110:        \"tip\": (1, 0),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:111:        \"tail\": (1, 2),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:115:        \"tip\": (1, 2),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:116:        \"tail\": (1, 0),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:120:    _spec[\"full\"] = set(_spec[\"body\"]) | {_spec[\"tip\"]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:161:def _tail_on_required_boundary(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:162:    tail: tuple[int, int], d: tuple[int, int], H: int, W: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:164:    r, c = tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:184:            tip_neighbors: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:192:                            tip_neighbors.add((rr, cc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:193:            if len(tip_neighbors) != 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:196:            tip = next(iter(tip_neighbors))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:197:            tip_col = int(g[tip])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:198:            full = set(body) | {tip}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:209:                expected_tip = (origin[0] + spec[\"tip\"][0], origin[1] + spec[\"tip\"][1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:210:                tail = (origin[0] + spec[\"tail\"][0], origin[1] + spec[\"tail\"][1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:211:                if tip != expected_tip:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:213:                if not _tail_on_required_boundary(tail, d, H, W):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:215:                matches.append((d, expected_tip, tail))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:219:            d, tip_rc, tail_rc = matches[0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:223:                    \"tip_col\": int(tip_col),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:225:                    \"tip\": tip_rc,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:226:                    \"tail\": tail_rc,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:429:    tr, tc = spec[\"tip\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:448:    tip = (r0 + spec[\"tip\"][0], c0 + spec[\"tip\"][1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:450:    return patch, r0, c0, tip, full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:579:    Build a red activation network whose first launch comes from a small arrow and whose rays curl clockwise into spirals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:584:    - The start marker is no longer a bottom stem; it is a boundary-anchored red arrow sprite with one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:585:      yellow protruding tip. The tip side reveals the initial firing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:588:    - Recolor the whole start arrow red, then launch a ray from the yellow tip in the direction implied\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:589:      by the arrow shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:597:    - Two cues must be read together: the arrow geometry gives the initial direction, and the repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:604:    # --- STEP 1) Detect the start arrow sprite and infer the initial direction ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:607:    yellow_col = int(start[\"tip_col\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:609:    start_tip = tuple(map(int, start[\"tip\"]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:694:    # --- STEP 5) Trace the arrow-launched spiral until it hits a blob or exhausts itself ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:706:    _trace_spiral_runtime(start_tip, start_dir, H, W, True, visit_ray)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:732:    # Place the directional start arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:734:    start_patch, start_r0, start_c0, start_tip, start_full = _start_placement(H, W, start_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:746:    current_start = start_tip\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
